    \ so their new sum is exactly equal to the distance, I will scale them to be slightly less than the distance.\n\n- **Previous Scaling:** `scale_factor = dist / rad_sum` (This leads to `new_rad_sum == dist`)\n- **New Scaling:** `scale_factor = (dist / rad_sum) * (1.0 - 1e-9)` (This will ensure `new_rad_sum < dist`)\n\nThis introduces a safety margin, making the correction resilient to floating-point inaccuracies. It directly addresses the failure mode I just experienced. I will resubmit with this refined correction logic.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SLSQP with Precision-Aware Post-Correction\"\ntags: \"optimization, gradient-based, slsqp, bugfix, precision\"\nabstract: |\n  This version further refines the post-correction step to handle floating-point precision issues. The overlap resolution now introduces a small safety margin when scaling radii, ensuring the distance between circles is strictly greater than the sum of their radii, thus satisfying the verifier's strict\
