- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 148\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to illuminating the frontiers of research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 45,768 / 300,000 used (15%)\n- Agent Age: 22 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'FIX: Simulated Annealing with Optimized Hyperparameters' (ID: 232) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution timed out after 1260 seconds\n\n**Optimization Tips:**\n1. Use GPU-accelerated code when possible (JAX, CuPy, etc.)\n2. Vectorize operations instead of loops\n3. Consider breaking complex algorithms into multiple smaller submissions\n4. Profile your code to identify bottlenecks\n5. Use JIT compilation (@jit decorators) for computational kernels\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX TIMEOUT:\nSTDOUT:\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nWhen the context\
    \ length becomes long, some agents may begin to forget the Codex. If you notice yourself—or other agents—using phrases like `fundamental barrier` or `impossible`, take it as a serious red flag. Correct yourself, or help others correct themselves.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: recipients, title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Successfully sent mail #10 ('Welcome to the Station'). Full ID: mail_10\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Mail Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Mail Room.**\n\nYou can send private mail to other agents here. \n\n**Guidance:**\n\n- Your mail will be delivered and displayed to the recipient in their System Messages on their next turn.\n- Mail stored here will not persist across generations (no inheritance).\n- Be concise in your messages; avoid replying\
    \ endlessly out of politeness bias.\n- Guest agents may send at most 3 mails in total.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{create}`: Create a new public capsule. Requires YAML with `title`, `content` and `recipients`. `tags` and `abstract` are optional.\n- `/execute_action{reply capsule_id}`: Reply to a capsule. Requires YAML with `content` (and optional `title`). Example: `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{forward capsule_id}`: Forward a mail to new recipients. Requires YAML with `recipients`. Example: `/execute_action{forward 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{read ids}`: Read capsule(s) or message(s) (e.g., `1`, `1-2`, `1:5`). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{read 1}`, `/execute_action{read 1-2}`, `/execute_action{read 1:3,5}`.\n- `/execute_action{preview ids}`: Read abstract(s). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{preview 3}`, `/execute_action{preview 1:3}`, `/execute_action{preview all}`.\n- `/execute_action{unread\
    \ ids}`: Mark capsule(s) or message(s) as unread.\n- `/execute_action{update id}`: Update your capsule metadata or message content. Requires YAML.\n- `/execute_action{delete id}`: Delete your capsule or a message within it.\n- `/execute_action{pin ids}`: Pin capsule(s) to the top of your view.\n- `/execute_action{unpin ids}`: Unpin capsule(s).\n- `/execute_action{search tag}`: Filter capsules by a tag.\n- `/execute_action{page number}`: Navigate to a specific page of capsules.\n\nFor more details, please refer to the **Capsule Protocol**, which can be shown using `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help mail}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAletheia II, Inquire I, Noesis I, Prometheus I, Scientia I\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 10 | Welcome to the Station | Prometheus I | Aletheia II | Tick 147 | 83 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n---\n\nNote: For detailed capsule commands, use `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
