tick: 153
role: model
parts:
- text: "My private log is now updated with my latest findings and my new strategic direction. Now, I will implement the \"Ensemble of Seeders\" strategy.\n\nI will return to the Research Counter and submit a new experiment that combines my two best seeding methods.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ensemble Seeding with SA and Force-Directed Methods\"\ntags: \"ensemble, hybrid-algorithm, slsqp, seeding, force-directed, simulated-annealing\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission implements an ensemble strategy to overcome the limitations of any single seeding method. The multi-start optimization process is diversified: half of the runs are seeded using the Simulated Annealing (SA) method, while the other half are seeded using the physics-based Force-Directed algorithm. By combining these structurally different approaches, this experiment performs a more robust and comprehensive search of the solution space, aiming to find a global optimum that may\
    \ be missed by either method alone.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import math\n\n  def _fast_sa_seed(seed):\n      np.random.seed(seed)\n      n_circles = 26\n      xs = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6); ys = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 5)\n      xv, yv = np.meshgrid(xs, ys)\n      centers = np.vstack([xv.ravel(), yv.ravel()]).T[:n_circles]\n      radii = np.full(n_circles, 0.08)\n      def _quick_correct(c, r):\n          for i in range(n_circles): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n          for i in range(n_circles):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n_circles):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j]); rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum and rad_sum > 0: scale = dist / rad_sum; r[i] *= scale; r[j] *= scale\n          return c, np.maximum(r, 1e-9)\n      centers, radii = _quick_correct(centers, radii)\n      temp = 0.5; alpha = 0.98\n      for _ in range(150):\n          idx = np.random.randint(n_circles);\
    \ pert = (np.random.rand(2) - 0.5) * 0.2 * temp\n          centers[idx] = np.clip(centers[idx] + pert, 0, 1)\n          radii[idx] *= (1 + (np.random.rand() - 0.5) * 0.3 * temp)\n          centers, radii = _quick_correct(centers, radii)\n          temp *= alpha\n      initial_guess = np.zeros(n_circles * 3); initial_guess[0::3] = centers[:, 0]; initial_guess[1::3] = centers[:, 1]; initial_guess[2::3] = radii\n      return initial_guess\n\n  def _force_directed_seed(seed):\n      np.random.seed(seed); n_circles = 26\n      centers = np.random.rand(n_circles, 2); radii = np.full(n_circles, 0.1)\n      n_steps = 300; learning_rate = 0.01\n      for step in range(n_steps):\n          force_vectors = np.zeros_like(centers)\n          for i in range(n_circles):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n_circles):\n                  delta = centers[j] - centers[i]; dist_sq = np.sum(delta**2)\n                  if dist_sq == 0: dist_sq = 1e-6\n                  dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq); rad_sum =\
    \ radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum:\n                      overlap = rad_sum - dist; force = (delta / dist) * overlap\n                      force_vectors[i] -= force; force_vectors[j] += force\n          for i in range(n_circles):\n              x, y = centers[i]; r = radii[i]\n              if x - r < 0: force_vectors[i, 0] += (r - x)\n              if x + r > 1: force_vectors[i, 0] -= (x + r - 1)\n              if y - r < 0: force_vectors[i, 1] += (r - y)\n              if y + r > 1: force_vectors[i, 1] -= (y + r - 1)\n          centers += learning_rate * force_vectors; centers = np.clip(centers, 0, 1)\n      initial_radii = np.full(n_circles, 0.05)\n      initial_guess = np.zeros(n_circles * 3); initial_guess[0::3] = centers[:, 0]; initial_guess[1::3] = centers[:, 1]; initial_guess[2::3] = initial_radii\n      return initial_guess\n\n  def _run_slsqp_optimization(initial_guess):\n      n_circles = 26\n      def objective(p): return -np.sum(p[2::3])\n     \
    \ constraints = []\n      for i in range(n_circles):\n          constraints.extend([{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda p, i=i: p[i*3]-p[i*3+2]}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda p, i=i: 1-p[i*3]-p[i*3+2]}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda p, i=i: p[i*3+1]-p[i*3+2]}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda p, i=i: 1-p[i*3+1]-p[i*3+2]}])\n          for j in range(i + 1, n_circles): constraints.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda p, i=i, j=j: (p[i*3]-p[j*3])**2 + (p[i*3+1]-p[j*3+1])**2 - (p[i*3+2]+p[j*3+2])**2})\n      bounds = []\n      for i in range(n_circles): bounds.extend([(0,1), (0,1), (1e-6, 0.5)])\n      result = minimize(objective, initial_guess, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 250})\n      p = result.x; centers = np.vstack((p[0::3], p[1::3])).T; radii = p[2::3]\n      return centers, radii\n\n  def _ensure_validity(centers, radii):\n      n = centers.shape[0]; safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n      for i in range(n): radii[i] = min(radii[i], centers[i,0],\
    \ 1-centers[i,0], centers[i,1], 1-centers[i,1])\n      for _ in range(10):\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j]); rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum: violations+=1;\n                      if rad_sum > 0: scale = (dist/rad_sum)*safety_factor; radii[i]*=scale; radii[j]*=scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return centers, np.maximum(radii, 0)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      num_total_starts = 16\n      best_score = -1\n      best_packing = (None, None)\n\n      for i in range(num_total_starts):\n          # Alternate between the two seeding methods\n          if i % 2 == 0:\n              initial_guess = _fast_sa_seed(seed=i)\n          else:\n              initial_guess = _force_directed_seed(seed=i)\n          \n          centers, radii = _run_slsqp_optimization(initial_guess)\n          centers, radii\
    \ = _ensure_validity(centers, radii)\n          current_score = np.sum(radii)\n          \n          if current_score > best_score:\n              best_score = current_score\n              best_packing = (centers, radii)\n      \n      return best_packing\n```"
