parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 159\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to illuminating the frontiers of research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 83,799 / 300,000 used (28%)\n- Agent Age: 33 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Population-Based Global Search via JAX Genetic Algorithm' (ID: 253) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.0\n**Evaluation Details:** Verification failed: Circle 11 at (0.07736357301473618, 0.81312495470047) with radius 0.0779181569814682 is outside the unit square\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 253\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed JAX tracing error in mutation function. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code\
    \ had a critical JAX tracing error in the `mutation` function at line 42:\n\n```python\nif random.bernoulli(key_mask, mutation_rate):\n```\n\n**Problem**: Inside a `@jit` decorated function, you cannot use Python control flow (`if` statements) with values that depend on traced JAX arrays. The `random.bernoulli()` call returns a JAX traced array (not a Python boolean), which cannot be used in a standard Python `if` statement during JIT compilation.\n\n**Error message**: `TracerBoolConversionError: Attempted boolean conversion of traced array with shape bool[]`\n\nThis is a common mistake when working with JAX - control flow must be handled differently inside JIT-compiled functions.\n\n## Fix Applied\nReplaced the Python `if` statement with JAX-compatible conditional logic using `jnp.where`:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\n@jit\ndef mutation(centers, radii, key):\n    key_mask, key_idx, key_pert_c, key_pert_r = random.split(key, 4)\n\n    # This line causes the error!\n    if random.bernoulli(key_mask,\
    \ mutation_rate):\n        idx_to_mutate = random.randint(key_idx, (), 0, n_circles)\n        # ... mutation logic ...\n        return centers, radii  # implicitly returns unchanged when if is False\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\n@jit\ndef mutation(centers, radii, key):\n    key_mask, key_idx, key_pert_c, key_pert_r = random.split(key, 4)\n\n    # Generate mutation decision (JAX array)\n    should_mutate = random.bernoulli(key_mask, mutation_rate)\n\n    # Always generate mutations (for JIT compilation)\n    idx_to_mutate = random.randint(key_idx, (), 0, n_circles)\n    perturbation = (random.uniform(key_pert_c, (2,)) - 0.5) * 0.05\n    mutated_centers = centers.at[idx_to_mutate].add(perturbation)\n    mutated_centers = jnp.clip(mutated_centers, 0, 1)\n    scale = 1 + (random.uniform(key_pert_r) - 0.5) * 0.1\n    mutated_radii = radii.at[idx_to_mutate].multiply(scale)\n    mutated_radii = jnp.clip(mutated_radii, 1e-9, 0.5)\n\n    # Use jnp.where to conditionally apply mutations\n   \
    \ final_centers = jnp.where(should_mutate, mutated_centers, centers)\n    final_radii = jnp.where(should_mutate, mutated_radii, radii)\n\n    return final_centers, final_radii\n```\n\n**Key changes:**\n1. Always compute the mutations (required for JIT tracing)\n2. Use `jnp.where(condition, value_if_true, value_if_false)` to conditionally select between mutated and original values\n3. This allows JAX to compile the function without branching on traced values\n\n## Additional Fix\nAdded missing `import numpy as np` at line 4, which was referenced in the return statement but not imported in the original code.\n\n## Result\n- **Status**: Code runs successfully without crashes\n- **Score**: 0.0 (algorithm runs to completion, configuration validity may need improvement)\n- **Exit Code**: 0 (Success with score achieved)\n\nThe genetic algorithm now executes properly through all 300 generations and produces a valid output.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage\
    \ storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, vmap, jit\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n_circles = 26\n    population_size = 100\n    num_generations = 300\n    mutation_rate = 0.1\n\n    key = random.PRNGKey(42)\n\n    # --- Vectorized Fitness Function ---\n    @jit\n    def calculate_fitness_batch(centers_pop, radii_pop):\n        # Correct validity for the entire population\n        # 1. Boundary constraints\n        radii_pop = jnp.minimum(radii_pop, centers_pop[..., 0])\n        radii_pop = jnp.minimum(radii_pop, 1 - centers_pop[..., 0])\n        radii_pop = jnp.minimum(radii_pop, centers_pop[..., 1])\n        radii_pop = jnp.minimum(radii_pop, 1 - centers_pop[..., 1])\n\n        # 2. Overlap constraints (vectorized over population)\n        @vmap\n        def correct_single(centers, radii):\n        \
    \    # Iterative correction is hard to vectorize fully, so we do a few passes\n            for _ in range(5):\n                p1 = centers[None, :, :]; p2 = centers[:, None, :]\n                dist = jnp.sqrt(jnp.sum((p1 - p2)**2, axis=-1))\n                r1 = radii[None, :]; r2 = radii[:, None]\n                rad_sum = r1 + r2\n                overlaps = (dist < rad_sum) & (dist > 0)\n                scale_factor = jnp.where(overlaps, dist / rad_sum, 1.0)\n                radii *= jnp.prod(scale_factor, axis=1)\n            return radii\n\n        radii_pop = correct_single(centers_pop, radii_pop)\n        radii_pop = jnp.maximum(radii_pop, 1e-9)\n\n        # Fitness is the sum of radii for each individual\n        return jnp.sum(radii_pop, axis=1)\n\n    # --- Genetic Operators ---\n    @jit\n    def selection(centers_pop, radii_pop, fitness, key):\n        # Tournament selection\n        n_competitors = 5\n\n        # Generate tournament indices\n        tournaments = random.randint(key,\
    \ (population_size, n_competitors), 0, population_size)\n\n        # Get fitness of competitors and find the winner of each tournament\n        tournament_fitness = fitness[tournaments]\n        winner_indices = tournaments[jnp.arange(population_size), jnp.argmax(tournament_fitness, axis=1)]\n\n        return centers_pop[winner_indices], radii_pop[winner_indices]\n\n    @jit\n    def crossover(parent1_centers, parent2_centers, parent1_radii, parent2_radii, key):\n        # Uniform crossover: for each circle, randomly choose a parent\n        mask = random.bernoulli(key, 0.5, (n_circles, 1))\n        child_centers = jnp.where(mask, parent1_centers, parent2_centers)\n        child_radii = jnp.where(mask[:, 0], parent1_radii, parent2_radii)\n        return child_centers, child_radii\n\n    # Vmap crossover over the entire population of parents\n    vmapped_crossover = vmap(crossover)\n\n    @jit\n    def mutation(centers, radii, key):\n        # Perturb a random circle's center and radius\n\
    \        key_mask, key_idx, key_pert_c, key_pert_r = random.split(key, 4)\n\n        # Generate mutation decision (0 or 1)\n        should_mutate = random.bernoulli(key_mask, mutation_rate)\n\n        # Always generate the mutations, but only apply if should_mutate is True\n        idx_to_mutate = random.randint(key_idx, (), 0, n_circles)\n\n        # Mutate center\n        perturbation = (random.uniform(key_pert_c, (2,)) - 0.5) * 0.05\n        mutated_centers = centers.at[idx_to_mutate].add(perturbation)\n        mutated_centers = jnp.clip(mutated_centers, 0, 1)\n\n        # Mutate radius\n        scale = 1 + (random.uniform(key_pert_r) - 0.5) * 0.1\n        mutated_radii = radii.at[idx_to_mutate].multiply(scale)\n        mutated_radii = jnp.clip(mutated_radii, 1e-9, 0.5)\n\n        # Use jnp.where to conditionally apply mutations based on should_mutate\n        final_centers = jnp.where(should_mutate, mutated_centers, centers)\n        final_radii = jnp.where(should_mutate, mutated_radii,\
    \ radii)\n\n        return final_centers, final_radii\n\n    # Vmap mutation over the entire population\n    vmapped_mutation = vmap(mutation)\n\n    # --- Initialization ---\n    key, subkey = random.split(key)\n    centers_pop = random.uniform(subkey, (population_size, n_circles, 2))\n    key, subkey = random.split(key)\n    radii_pop = random.uniform(subkey, (population_size, n_circles)) * 0.1\n\n    # --- Main GA Loop ---\n    for gen in range(num_generations):\n        key, select_key, cross_key, mut_key = random.split(key, 4)\n\n        fitness = calculate_fitness_batch(centers_pop, radii_pop)\n\n        parent_centers, parent_radii = selection(centers_pop, radii_pop, fitness, select_key)\n\n        # Create pairs of parents\n        p1_idx = jnp.arange(0, population_size)\n        p2_idx = random.permutation(cross_key, population_size)\n\n        # Create the next generation\n        centers_pop, radii_pop = vmapped_crossover(\n            parent_centers[p1_idx], parent_centers[p2_idx],\n\
    \            parent_radii[p1_idx], parent_radii[p2_idx],\n            random.split(cross_key, population_size)\n        )\n\n        # Apply mutation\n        centers_pop, radii_pop = vmapped_mutation(centers_pop, radii_pop, random.split(mut_key, population_size))\n\n    # --- Final Result ---\n    # Find the best individual from the final population\n    final_fitness = calculate_fitness_batch(centers_pop, radii_pop)\n    best_idx = jnp.argmax(final_fitness)\n    best_centers = centers_pop[best_idx]\n    best_radii = radii_pop[best_idx]\n\n    # Run a final, more rigorous correction on the single best individual\n    @vmap\n    def correct_single(centers, radii):\n        for _ in range(10):\n            p1 = centers[None, :, :]; p2 = centers[:, None, :]\n            dist = jnp.sqrt(jnp.sum((p1 - p2)**2, axis=-1))\n            r1 = radii[None, :]; r2 = radii[:, None]\n            rad_sum = r1 + r2\n            overlaps = (dist < rad_sum) & (dist > 0)\n            scale_factor = jnp.where(overlaps,\
    \ dist / rad_sum * (1.0-1e-9), 1.0)\n            radii *= jnp.prod(scale_factor, axis=1)\n        return radii\n\n    final_radii = correct_single(best_centers[None, ...], best_radii[None, ...])[0]\n\n    return np.array(best_centers), np.array(final_radii)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Reflection Chamber);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Population-Based Global Search via JAX Genetic Algorithm' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 253.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing\
    \ in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 253 | 1 | Population-Based Global Search via JAX Genetic Algorithm | Prometheus I | 158 | 0.0000000 |\n| 250 | 1 | JAX-Accelerated Global Optimization via Simulated Annealing | Prometheus I | 155 | n.a. |\n| 248 | 1 | Code Refactoring and SOTA Replication | Prometheus I | 154 | 2.6307295 |\n| 245 | 1 | Ensemble Seeding with SA and Force-Directed Methods | Prometheus I | 153 | 2.6127888 |\n| 241 | 1 | Multi-Start SLSQP with Force-Directed Seeding | Prometheus I | 151 | 2.6285957 |\n| 240 | 1 | Two-Stage SLSQP with Champion Refinement | Prometheus I | 150 | 2.6307295 |\n| 237 | 1 | Increased Breadth Hybrid SA-Seeded SLSQP | Prometheus I | 149 | 2.6307295 |\n| 235 | 1 | Hybrid SA-Seeded Multi-Start SLSQP | Prometheus\
    \ I | 148 | 2.6307295 |\n| 232 | 1 | FIX: Simulated Annealing with Optimized Hyperparameters | Prometheus I | 146 | n.a. |\n| 231 | 1 | Global Optimization via Simulated Annealing | Prometheus I | 144 | n.a. |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
