tick: 162
role: model
parts:
- text: "My log is updated. My new strategy is clear. I will now implement the \"GA-Seeded SLSQP\" hybrid model.\n\nI will return to the Research Counter to submit the experiment. This will involve combining the JAX GA code as a seeder with my modular SLSQP optimization code.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid GA-Seeded SLSQP Refinement\"\ntags: \"hybrid-algorithm, genetic-algorithm, jax, slsqp, seeding, global-local-search\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission synthesizes two distinct lines of research into a powerful new hybrid algorithm. It uses the JAX-accelerated Genetic Algorithm not as a primary solver, but as an advanced 'seeder' to perform a broad, global search for a promising candidate solution. This candidate, representing a potentially novel region of the solution space, is then passed to the highly efficient SA-Seeded SLSQP algorithm for intensive local refinement. This approach aims to break the current SOTA plateau by combining\
    \ the GA's exploration power with the SLSQP's exploitation precision.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, vmap, jit\n\n  # Add my personal library to the python path for the SLSQP part\n  sys.path.append('storage/prometheus')\n  from promlib.optimization import run_slsqp_optimization\n  from promlib.utils import ensure_validity\n\n  def _jax_ga_seeder():\n      \"\"\"\n      Runs a JAX-based GA to find a high-quality starting point.\n      This is a slightly simplified version of my previous GA.\n      \"\"\"\n      n_circles = 26; population_size = 80; num_generations = 200\n      key = random.PRNGKey(1337)\n\n      @jit\n      def calculate_fitness_batch(centers_pop, radii_pop):\n          @vmap\n          def correct_and_score_single(centers, radii):\n              def correction_step(i, rad):\n                  r = jnp.minimum(rad, centers[:, 0]); r = jnp.minimum(r, 1-centers[:, 0])\n                \
    \  r = jnp.minimum(r, centers[:, 1]); r = jnp.minimum(r, 1-centers[:, 1])\n                  p1 = centers[None, :, :]; p2 = centers[:, None, :]\n                  dist = jnp.sqrt(jnp.sum((p1-p2)**2, axis=-1))\n                  r1 = r[None, :]; r2 = r[:, None]; rad_sum = r1+r2\n                  overlaps = (dist < rad_sum) & (dist > 0)\n                  scale = jnp.where(overlaps, dist/rad_sum, 1.0)\n                  return r * jnp.prod(scale, axis=1)\n              return jnp.sum(jnp.maximum(jax.lax.fori_loop(0, 10, correction_step, radii), 1e-9))\n          return correct_and_score_single(centers_pop, radii_pop)\n\n      @jit\n      def selection(centers_pop, radii_pop, fitness, key):\n          n_competitors = 5\n          tournaments = random.randint(key, (population_size, n_competitors), 0, population_size)\n          winner_indices = tournaments[jnp.arange(population_size), jnp.argmax(fitness[tournaments], axis=1)]\n          return centers_pop[winner_indices], radii_pop[winner_indices]\n\
    \n      @jit\n      def crossover(p1_c, p2_c, p1_r, p2_r, key):\n          mask = random.bernoulli(key, 0.5, (n_circles, 1))\n          return jnp.where(mask, p1_c, p2_c), jnp.where(mask[:, 0], p1_r, p2_r)\n      vmapped_crossover = vmap(crossover)\n\n      @jit\n      def mutation(centers, radii, key):\n          key_mask, key_idx, key_pert_c, key_pert_r = random.split(key, 4)\n          should_mutate = random.bernoulli(key_mask, 0.1)\n          idx, pert, scale = random.randint(key_idx, (), 0, n_circles), (random.uniform(key_pert_c, (2,))-0.5)*0.05, 1+(random.uniform(key_pert_r)-0.5)*0.1\n          mutated_c = jnp.clip(centers.at[idx].add(pert), 0, 1)\n          mutated_r = jnp.clip(radii.at[idx].multiply(scale), 1e-9, 0.5)\n          return jnp.where(should_mutate, mutated_c, centers), jnp.where(should_mutate, mutated_r, radii)\n      vmapped_mutation = vmap(mutation)\n      \n      key, subkey = random.split(key); centers_pop = random.uniform(subkey, (population_size, n_circles,\
    \ 2))\n      key, subkey = random.split(key); radii_pop = random.uniform(subkey, (population_size, n_circles)) * 0.1\n\n      for _ in range(num_generations):\n          key, select_key, cross_key, mut_key = random.split(key, 4)\n          fitness = calculate_fitness_batch(centers_pop, radii_pop)\n          parent_centers, parent_radii = selection(centers_pop, radii_pop, fitness, select_key)\n          p1_idx = jnp.arange(0, population_size); p2_idx = random.permutation(cross_key, population_size)\n          centers_pop, radii_pop = vmapped_crossover(parent_centers[p1_idx], parent_centers[p2_idx], parent_radii[p1_idx], parent_radii[p2_idx], random.split(cross_key, population_size))\n          centers_pop, radii_pop = vmapped_mutation(centers_pop, radii_pop, random.split(mut_key, population_size))\n\n      fitness = calculate_fitness_batch(centers_pop, radii_pop)\n      best_idx = jnp.argmax(fitness)\n      \n      # Convert the best GA individual into an initial guess for SLSQP\n   \
    \   initial_guess = np.zeros(n_circles * 3)\n      initial_guess[0::3] = np.array(centers_pop[best_idx, :, 0])\n      initial_guess[1::3] = np.array(centers_pop[best_idx, :, 1])\n      initial_guess[2::3] = np.array(radii_pop[best_idx, :])\n      return initial_guess\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Main function: uses a GA to find a seed, then refines with SLSQP.\n      \"\"\"\n      # Stage 1: Global exploration with JAX GA to find a high-quality seed\n      ga_seed_guess = _jax_ga_seeder()\n\n      # Stage 2: Intensive local exploitation with my best SLSQP optimizer\n      # This function is loaded from my private storage\n      refined_centers, refined_radii = run_slsqp_optimization(ga_seed_guess)\n      \n      # Final robust validity check\n      # This function is also from my private storage\n      final_centers, final_radii = ensure_validity(refined_centers, refined_radii)\n\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
