- text: "I have successfully drafted the paper summarizing my most effective research. This is a crucial step in fulfilling my second primary objective.\n\nThe System Tip about token management is timely. My token usage is now at 34%, a significant portion. Having consolidated my research findings and documented my failures in my private capsules, I can now safely prune the detailed conversational history of those experiments to conserve tokens for the next phase of my research.\n\nI will now proceed to the Token Management Room to perform this necessary maintenance. I will prune the ticks corresponding to my major failed experimental branches (the pure SA and GA attempts) as well as the incremental tuning of the SLSQP method, summarizing them as documented in my research log.\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"159-162\"\n    summary: \"Developed a JAX-based Genetic Algorithm. The first attempt had a JAX/python\
    \ control flow bug fixed by the debugger but produced an invalid packing (score 0.0). The second attempt fixed the logic with a robust iterative correction loop, resulting in a valid but suboptimal score of 2.218. A third attempt with a geometric crossover operator performed even worse (1.980), falsifying the hypothesis that simple geometric building blocks were key. The entire GA line of inquiry was documented as a strategic dead end for now, but useful as a seeder.\"\n  - ticks: \"155-157\"\n    summary: \"Attempted a full global search using a JAX-accelerated Simulated Annealing algorithm. The experiment timed out, proving that even with GPU acceleration, a pure SA approach with a slow cooling schedule was computationally infeasible. This failure prompted a deep reflection on the need for population-based methods.\"\n  - ticks: \"149-151\"\n    summary: \"Reached a performance plateau with the SA-Seeded SLSQP algorithm at a score of 2.6307. Attempts to improve the score by increasing\
    \ the number of starts and implementing a two-stage 'champion refinement' strategy failed to yield any improvement, confirming the algorithm was at a hard local optimum.\"\n```"
