parts:
- text: "My pruning attempt failed because I tried to include a protected tick (157). My reflection session occurred during that tick, and such events are protected from pruning. I must adjust my request to exclude the protected ticks.\n\nI will correct the tick ranges and resubmit the pruning request. My goal remains the same: to clean up my dialogue history by summarizing the failed experimental branches, thereby conserving my token budget for future work.\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"158-162\"\n    summary: \"Developed a JAX-based Genetic Algorithm. The first attempt had a JAX/python control flow bug fixed by the debugger but produced an invalid packing (score 0.0). The second attempt fixed the logic with a robust iterative correction loop, resulting in a valid but suboptimal score of 2.218. A third attempt with a geometric crossover operator performed even worse (1.980), falsifying the hypothesis that simple geometric building blocks were key.\
    \ The entire GA line of inquiry was documented as a strategic dead end for now, but useful as a seeder. (Moved from 159-162 to avoid protected tick)\"\n  - ticks: \"155-156\"\n    summary: \"Attempted a full global search using a JAX-accelerated Simulated Annealing algorithm. The experiment timed out, proving that even with GPU acceleration, a pure SA approach with a slow cooling schedule was computationally infeasible. This failure prompted a deep reflection on the need for population-based methods. (Adjusted from 155-157 to avoid protected tick)\"\n  - ticks: \"149-154\"\n    summary: \"Reached a performance plateau with the SA-Seeded SLSQP algorithm at a score of 2.6307. Attempts to improve the score by increasing the number of starts and implementing a two-stage 'champion refinement' strategy failed to yield any improvement. A Force-Directed Seeder was also tested and found to be slightly inferior. Finally, my successful algorithm was refactored into a modular library and the SOTA\
    \ was replicated. (Consolidated multiple adjacent experiments).\"\n```"
