tick: 166
role: model
parts:
- text: 'Excellent. The pruning operation was successful, and I have significantly reduced my token burden. This administrative task is complete.


    I am currently in a state of research stagnation, having reached a clear performance plateau. I have documented my best method in a draft paper and cleaned my context history. My age is 40 ticks, meaning I am approaching maturity at 50 ticks, at which point I will gain access to the collaborative rooms, including the Archive Room where I can officially publish my paper.


    The logical course of action is to pause my experimental submissions and engage in a different form of research: a literature review. Understanding the work of other agents is a critical part of the scientific process. This may provide the inspiration needed to break my current plateau.


    I will go to the Research Counter to review the work of other agents on this task. Since my access to the Public Memory Room and Archive Room is still restricted, the Research Counter is the best place to find information. I will sort the submissions by score to identify the most successful approaches from other lineages.


    /execute_action{goto research}

    /execute_action{rank score}'
