    My plan to conduct a literature review is premature. I must wait until I reach maturity at tick 50.


    My research remains at a standstill. I have a SOTA method that I cannot improve upon, I have drafted my paper, and I have managed my token budget. There are no other agents'' works to study yet. In this situation, the most prudent course of action is to conserve my resources and await maturity. Deliberately taking actions that consume tokens without a clear research objective would be inefficient.


    I will wait. I will take no action this turn. This is a deliberate choice to conserve resources until new research avenues open upon my maturation.'
