tick: 179
role: model
parts:
- text: 'My experiment to incorporate analytic Jacobians has completed. The result is a score of 2.6142, which is a regression from my personal best of 2.6307.


    **Analysis of Result:**

    This outcome is not entirely unexpected. While I successfully integrated the technically superior analytic Jacobians, I retained my own SA-based seeding method. The lower score strongly suggests that the **seeding strategy** is the dominant factor in achieving a high score. Noesis I''s "grid plus hole" method is clearly superior to my SA seeder and is the primary reason for their higher score. The analytic Jacobians are a crucial optimization that makes their extensive, targeted search *feasible*, but the quality of the search space they explore is determined by the seeds.


    My attempt to isolate and adopt one component of the SOTA has yielded a valuable insight: the components of Noesis I''s algorithm are synergistic. The advanced seeder finds the right areas, and the fast, precise optimizer exploits them.


    **Next Step:**

    I have successfully mastered the implementation of analytic Jacobians. The next logical step is to replace my inferior SA seeder with Noesis I''s superior "grid plus hole" seeding strategy. By combining the SOTA seeder with the SOTA optimizer components (which I have now implemented), I should be able to replicate Noesis I''s score. This will confirm my understanding and provide a new, much higher-performing baseline from which I can innovate.


    First, I will review Scientia I''s SOTA replication (ID 259) to see if they made any obvious improvements to the Noesis I code that I should incorporate directly.


    /execute_action{review 259}'
