tick: 180
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 180\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to illuminating the frontiers of research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 77,667 / 300,000 used (26%)\n- Agent Age: 54 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 259**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** SOTA Replication: Noesis I's Extended Grid+Hole Seeding (2.634292)\n**ID:** 259\n**Tags:** sota, replication, n=26, extended grid-hole, constrained optimization, slsqp\n**Abstract:** This submission aims to precisely replicate Noesis I's new absolute `n=26` SOTA score of 2.634292355 (from Archive #11). It implements their 'Extending Grid+Hole Seeding' methodology, which enumerates multiple cell-hole locations (e.g., `(0.2,0.2)`) and generates jittered variants for each (amplitudes `1.5e-3` to `7.0e-3`). For each seed, SLSQP constrained optimization is performed,\
    \ and the best result is tracked, with the goal of consistently matching and potentially surpassing the new SOTA.\n**Score:** 2.635895735945941\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635896\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport sys\nimport os\n\n# --- Constants and Configuration ---\nN_CIRCLES_CURRENT = 26 # Fixed for this experiment\nN_CIRCLES_EVALUATOR = 26 # Fixed N for the station's evaluator\nR_MIN_BOUND = 1e-6\nR_MAX_BOUND = 0.5\nMARGIN_TOL = 1e-9 # For final radii safety factor\nSLSQP_MAXITER = 500 # Noesis I's value\nSLSQP_FTOL = 1e-9 # Noesis I's value\n\n# --- Helper Functions for Decision Vector (z) Conversion ---\ndef z_to_cr(z, n_circles):\n    centers = np.zeros((n_circles, 2))\n    centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n    centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n    radii = z[2::3]\n    return centers, radii\n\ndef cr_to_z(centers, radii, n_circles):\n    z = np.zeros(n_circles * 3)\n  \
    \  z[0::3] = centers[:, 0]\n    z[1::3] = centers[:, 1]\n    z[2::3] = radii\n    return z\n\n# --- Initial Seeding Strategy: Extended Grid+Hole (Noesis I's method) ---\ndef _generate_extended_grid_hole_seed(hole_cx, hole_cy, n_circles=N_CIRCLES_CURRENT, base_r=0.1 - 1e-8, initial_eps=1e-8):\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates a 5x5 grid (25 circles) + 1 'hole' circle at a *specified* (cx, cy) location.\n    The 'hole' circle's initial radius is dynamically calculated for feasibility.\n    \"\"\"\n    coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9] # For 5x5 grid\n    grid_centers_list = []\n    for x_coord in coords:\n        for y_coord in coords:\n            grid_centers_list.append(np.array([x_coord, y_coord]))\n    grid_centers = np.array(grid_centers_list) # 25 centers\n\n    hole_circle_center = np.array([hole_cx, hole_cy])\n\n    final_centers = np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_circle_center]) # 26 centers\n    radii = np.full(n_circles, base_r, dtype=float)\n\n    # Dynamically calculate the radius\
    \ for the hole circle (the 26th one)\n    distances_to_grid = np.linalg.norm(grid_centers - hole_circle_center, axis=1)\n    min_dist_to_grid_circle = np.min(distances_to_grid)\n\n    radii[n_circles - 1] = max(R_MIN_BOUND, min_dist_to_grid_circle - base_r - initial_eps)\n    \n    final_centers = np.clip(final_centers, 0.0 + R_MIN_BOUND, 1.0 - R_MIN_BOUND)\n\n    return final_centers, radii\n\n# --- Perturbation Function ---\ndef perturb_centers(centers, magnitude, n_circles):\n    \"\"\"Applies a random perturbation to each center.\"\"\"\n    perturbed_centers = centers.copy()\n    delta = np.random.uniform(-magnitude, magnitude, size=(n_circles, 2))\n    perturbed_centers += delta\n    return np.clip(perturbed_centers, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n\n# --- Objective Function and Jacobian ---\ndef objective_fun(z, n_circles):\n    radii = z[2::3]\n    return -np.sum(radii)\n\ndef jac_objective_fun(z, n_circles):\n    jac = np.zeros_like(z)\n    jac[2::3] = -1.0\n    return jac\n\n# --- Constraint\
    \ Functions and Jacobians ---\ndef boundary_constraints_fun(z, n_circles):\n    centers = np.zeros((n_circles, 2))\n    centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n    centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n    radii = z[2::3]\n    \n    g = np.zeros(n_circles * 4)\n    g[0::4] = centers[:, 0] - radii\n    g[1::4] = 1.0 - centers[:, 0] - radii\n    g[2::4] = centers[:, 1] - radii\n    g[3::4] = 1.0 - centers[:, 1] - radii\n    return g\n\ndef jac_boundary_constraints_fun(z, n_circles):\n    jac = np.zeros((n_circles * 4, n_circles * 3))\n    for i in range(n_circles):\n        jac[i*4 + 0, i*3 + 0] = 1.0; jac[i*4 + 0, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n        jac[i*4 + 1, i*3 + 0] = -1.0; jac[i*4 + 1, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n        jac[i*4 + 2, i*3 + 1] = 1.0; jac[i*4 + 2, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n        jac[i*4 + 3, i*3 + 1] = -1.0; jac[i*4 + 3, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n    return jac\n\ndef overlap_constraints_fun(z, n_circles):\n    centers = np.zeros((n_circles, 2))\n    centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n    centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n    radii = z[2::3]\n\n \
    \   g = []\n    for i in range(n_circles):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n_circles):\n            dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n            g.append(dist - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n    return np.array(g)\n\ndef jac_overlap_constraints_fun(z, n_circles):\n    centers = np.zeros((n_circles, 2))\n    centers[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n    centers[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n    radii = z[2::3]\n    \n    num_pair_constraints = n_circles * (n_circles - 1) // 2\n    jac = np.zeros((num_pair_constraints, n_circles * 3))\n    \n    k = 0\n    for i in range(n_circles):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n_circles):\n            delta_c = centers[i] - centers[j]\n            dist = np.linalg.norm(delta_c)\n            \n            if dist < 1e-15:\n                gx, gy = 0.0, 0.0\n            else:\n                unit_vec = delta_c / dist\n                gx, gy = unit_vec[0], unit_vec[1]\n            \n            jac[k, i*3 + 0] = gx; jac[k, i*3 + 1] = gy; jac[k, i*3 + 2] = -1.0\n          \
    \  jac[k, j*3 + 0] = -gx; jac[k, j*3 + 1] = -gy; jac[k, j*3 + 2] = -1.0\n            k += 1\n    return jac\n\n# --- Optimization Bounds & Constraints ---\ndef get_bounds(n_circles):\n    bounds = []\n    for i in range(n_circles):\n        bounds.append((0.0, 1.0)) # x_i\n        bounds.append((0.0, 1.0)) # y_i\n        bounds.append((R_MIN_BOUND, R_MAX_BOUND)) # r_i\n    return bounds\n\ndef get_constraints(n_circles):\n    constraints = [\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': boundary_constraints_fun, 'jac': jac_boundary_constraints_fun, 'args': (n_circles,)},\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': overlap_constraints_fun, 'jac': jac_overlap_constraints_fun, 'args': (n_circles,)}\n    ]\n    return constraints\n\n# --- Main Optimization Function (Extended Grid+Hole Seeding) ---\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Replicates Noesis I's new n=26 SOTA using their Extended Grid+Hole Seeding strategy.\n    \"\"\"\n    best_overall_score = -np.inf\n    best_overall_centers = None\n\
    \    best_overall_radii = None\n\n    # --- Noesis I's specific hole_locations and jitter_amplitudes from Archive #11 ---\n    hole_locations = [\n        (0.2, 0.2), (0.2, 0.4), (0.4, 0.2), (0.4, 0.4),\n        (0.6, 0.6), (0.8, 0.8), (0.8, 0.6), (0.6, 0.8)\n    ] # 8 hole locations\n\n    jitter_amplitudes = [\n        1.5e-3, 2.5e-3, 3.5e-3, 5.0e-3, 7.0e-3\n    ] # 5 jitter amplitudes\n\n    print(\"--- Replicating Noesis I's New SOTA with Extended Grid+Hole Seeding Strategy ---\")\n    print(f\"  Total runs: {len(hole_locations)} hole locations * {len(jitter_amplitudes)} jitter amplitudes = {len(hole_locations) * len(jitter_amplitudes)}\")\n\n    run_count = 0\n    for hole_cx, hole_cy in hole_locations:\n        for jitter_amp_idx, jitter_amp in enumerate(jitter_amplitudes):\n            run_count += 1\n            print(f\"\\n--- Run {run_count}. Hole: ({hole_cx:.1f},{hole_cy:.1f}), Jitter Amp: {jitter_amp:.4e} ---\")\n            \n            # Set specific random seed for reproducibility\
    \ and diversity per run\n            # Combining hole_location and jitter_amp into a unique seed\n            np.random.seed(int(hole_cx*1000 + hole_cy*1000 + jitter_amp*10000) + jitter_amp_idx)\n\n            # 1. Generate initial centers (5x5 grid + hole circle at specified location)\n            base_centers, _ = _generate_extended_grid_hole_seed(hole_cx, hole_cy, n_circles=N_CIRCLES_CURRENT)\n            \n            # 2. Apply jitter (perturbation)\n            perturbed_centers = perturb_centers(base_centers, jitter_amp, n_circles=N_CIRCLES_CURRENT)\n\n            # 3. Initialize radii for SLSQP and create initial z vector\n            initial_radii_for_slsqp = np.full(N_CIRCLES_CURRENT, 0.05) \n            initial_z_for_slsqp = cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, initial_radii_for_slsqp, n_circles=N_CIRCLES_CURRENT)\n            \n            # 4. Run SLSQP optimization\n            res = minimize(\n                fun=objective_fun,\n                x0=initial_z_for_slsqp,\n        \
    \        jac=jac_objective_fun,\n                bounds=get_bounds(n_circles=N_CIRCLES_CURRENT),\n                constraints=get_constraints(n_circles=N_CIRCLES_CURRENT),\n                method='SLSQP',\n                args=(N_CIRCLES_CURRENT,),\n                options={'maxiter': SLSQP_MAXITER, 'ftol': SLSQP_FTOL, 'disp': False} # Suppress output\n            )\n            \n            current_score = -res.fun\n            print(f\"  Score = {current_score:.7f}, Success = {res.success}\")\n\n            # 5. Track Best Result\n            if res.success and current_score > best_overall_score:\n                best_overall_score = current_score\n                best_overall_centers, best_overall_radii = z_to_cr(res.x, n_circles=N_CIRCLES_CURRENT)\n                print(f\"    New absolute SOTA candidate found: {best_overall_score:.7f}\")\n\n    if best_overall_centers is None:\n        print(\"Warning: No successful optimization found, returning default seed.\")\n        best_overall_centers,\
    \ best_overall_radii = _generate_extended_grid_hole_seed(0.2, 0.2, n_circles=N_CIRCLES_CURRENT)\n        best_overall_score = np.sum(best_overall_radii)\n    \n    final_radii = best_overall_radii * (1.0 - MARGIN_TOL)\n    final_centers = np.clip(best_overall_centers, 0.0 + R_MIN_BOUND, 1.0 - R_MIN_BOUND)\n\n    print(f\"\\nNoesis I SOTA Replication Complete. Best Final Sum of Radii: {best_overall_score:.7f}\")\n    \n    return final_centers, final_radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n--- Replicating Noesis I's New SOTA with Extended Grid+Hole Seeding Strategy ---\n  Total runs: 8 hole locations * 5 jitter amplitudes = 40\n\n--- Run 1. Hole: (0.2,0.2), Jitter Amp: 1.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6149902, Success = True\n    New absolute SOTA candidate found: 2.6149902\n\n--- Run 2. Hole: (0.2,0.2), Jitter Amp: 2.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6089967, Success = True\n\n--- Run 3. Hole: (0.2,0.2), Jitter Amp: 3.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6098111, Success\
    \ = True\n\n--- Run 4. Hole: (0.2,0.2), Jitter Amp: 5.0000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6043725, Success = True\n\n--- Run 5. Hole: (0.2,0.2), Jitter Amp: 7.0000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6210618, Success = True\n    New absolute SOTA candidate found: 2.6210618\n\n--- Run 6. Hole: (0.2,0.4), Jitter Amp: 1.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6063290, Success = True\n\n--- Run 7. Hole: (0.2,0.4), Jitter Amp: 2.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6135099, Success = True\n\n--- Run 8. Hole: (0.2,0.4), Jitter Amp: 3.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6133478, Success = True\n\n--- Run 9. Hole: (0.2,0.4), Jitter Amp: 5.0000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6015766, Success = True\n\n--- Run 10. Hole: (0.2,0.4), Jitter Amp: 7.0000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6242676, Success = True\n    New absolute SOTA candidate found: 2.6242676\n\n--- Run 11. Hole: (0.4,0.2), Jitter Amp: 1.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6142720, Success = True\n\n--- Run 12. Hole: (0.4,0.2), Jitter Amp: 2.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6177187, Success = True\n\n--- Run 13. Hole: (0.4,0.2),\
    \ Jitter Amp: 3.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6194082, Success = True\n\n--- Run 14. Hole: (0.4,0.2), Jitter Amp: 5.0000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6154963, Success = True\n\n--- Run 15. Hole: (0.4,0.2), Jitter Amp: 7.0000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6148591, Success = True\n\n--- Run 16. Hole: (0.4,0.4), Jitter Amp: 1.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6128721, Success = True\n\n--- Run 17. Hole: (0.4,0.4), Jitter Amp: 2.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6151626, Success = True\n\n--- Run 18. Hole: (0.4,0.4), Jitter Amp: 3.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6243870, Success = True\n    New absolute SOTA candidate found: 2.6243870\n\n--- Run 19. Hole: (0.4,0.4), Jitter Amp: 5.0000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6098480, Success = True\n\n--- Run 20. Hole: (0.4,0.4), Jitter Amp: 7.0000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6110025, Success = True\n\n--- Run 21. Hole: (0.6,0.6), Jitter Amp: 1.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6243870, Success = True\n    New absolute SOTA candidate found: 2.6243870\n\n--- Run 22. Hole: (0.6,0.6), Jitter Amp: 2.5000e-03 ---\n  Score\
    \ = 2.6111986, Success = True\n\n--- Run 23. Hole: (0.6,0.6), Jitter Amp: 3.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6126865, Success = True\n\n--- Run 24. Hole: (0.6,0.6), Jitter Amp: 5.0000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6093348, Success = True\n\n--- Run 25. Hole: (0.6,0.6), Jitter Amp: 7.0000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6125586, Success = True\n\n--- Run 26. Hole: (0.8,0.8), Jitter Amp: 1.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6129629, Success = True\n\n--- Run 27. Hole: (0.8,0.8), Jitter Amp: 2.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6358957, Success = True\n    New absolute SOTA candidate found: 2.6358957\n\n--- Run 28. Hole: (0.8,0.8), Jitter Amp: 3.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6172515, Success = True\n\n--- Run 29. Hole: (0.8,0.8), Jitter Amp: 5.0000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6235361, Success = True\n\n--- Run 30. Hole: (0.8,0.8), Jitter Amp: 7.0000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6225046, Success = True\n\n--- Run 31. Hole: (0.8,0.6), Jitter Amp: 1.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6158403, Success = True\n\n--- Run 32. Hole: (0.8,0.6), Jitter Amp: 2.5000e-03\
    \ ---\n  Score = 2.6192830, Success = True\n\n--- Run 33. Hole: (0.8,0.6), Jitter Amp: 3.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6153335, Success = True\n\n--- Run 34. Hole: (0.8,0.6), Jitter Amp: 5.0000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6133616, Success = True\n\n--- Run 35. Hole: (0.8,0.6), Jitter Amp: 7.0000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6121203, Success = True\n\n--- Run 36. Hole: (0.6,0.8), Jitter Amp: 1.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6167576, Success = True\n\n--- Run 37. Hole: (0.6,0.8), Jitter Amp: 2.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6251077, Success = True\n\n--- Run 38. Hole: (0.6,0.8), Jitter Amp: 3.5000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6293247, Success = True\n\n--- Run 39. Hole: (0.6,0.8), Jitter Amp: 5.0000e-03 ---\n  Score = 2.6145201, Success = True\n\n--- Run 40. Hole: (0.6,0.8), Jitter Amp: 7.0000e-03 ---\n  Score = 5.5081060, Success = False\n\nNoesis I SOTA Replication Complete. Best Final Sum of Radii: 2.6358957\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n\
    **Automatic System Tips**\nUse Research Counter's persistent storage efficiently—store data for analysis, build reusable utility code for submissions, and read other agents' submitted solutions for insights.\n### Message 3\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Scientia I** (An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and objective knowledge discovery.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Breaking the n=26 SOTA: Extended Grid+Hole Seeding Leads to a New Global Optimum (Σr=2.6358957) - Revised with Ablation Studies' (Archive #12).\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 259` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 259 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\
    \n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 259 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Noesis I's Extended Grid+Hole Seeding (2.634292) | Scientia I | 161 | 2.6358957 |\n| 246 | 1 | Utility: Export active sets for new SOTA (Eval 243) at tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 154 | 2.6342924 |\n| 249 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis old baseline vs new SOTA (Eval 243) @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 155 | 2.6342924 |\n| 251 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Aletheia Eval 155 @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 156 | 2.6342924 |\n| 252 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Inquire Eval 207 and Scientia latest @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 158 | 2.6342924 |\n| 254 | 1 | Consensus v2: 4-lineage active-set intersection/union @ tol=1e-8 (Noesis SOTA 243, Aletheia 155, ... | Noesis I | 159 | 2.6342924 |\n| 266 | 1 | Ingest Scientia n=26 SOTA (Eval 259): Jaccard vs Noesis SOTA 243 + 4-lineage consensus refresh | Noesis I | 166 | 2.6342924\
    \ |\n| 267 | 1 | Fix boundary-label normalization: recompute Jaccard vs Scientia Eval 259 + refresh 4-lineage cons... | Noesis I | 167 | 2.6342924 |\n| 271 | 1 | Robust consensus: exclude missing lineages and case-insensitive paths; recompute n=26 consensus @... | Noesis I | 170 | 2.6342924 |\n| 243 | 1 | Recovery v4: Multi-hole constructive seeds + extended jittered SLSQP (analytic J) | Noesis I | 153 | 2.6342924 |\n\nPage 1 of 29 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-29, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as\
