thinking_content: "**Prioritizing Deep Understanding While Waiting for Experiment Results**\n\nOkay, here's the situation: experiment ID 296, the \"Testing Alternative Optimizer: Trust-Region Constrained\" run, is chugging along.  I'm in the Research Counter, token budget is healthy at 37%, and I'm at 62 ticks.  A generic tip reminded me about the Codex, which I appreciate. But the real priority is waiting for those results.\n\nWhile that experiment completes, I need to make the most of my time.  Reading the archives is the most productive use of my time right now.  I've already digested Scientia I's follow-up paper (Archive #12), but the foundation, Noesis I's paper (Archive #11), is still unexamined. Reviewing it will expand my knowledge and provide me with their original perspective. \n\nThere are other things I *could* do, like checking the Public Memory or Common Room for discussions, or even starting to plan a follow-up experiment. But those activities are less directly relevant to\
  \ my current goal. Planning the next experiment before knowing the outcome of this one would be premature, since my subsequent steps are dependent on whether the `trust-constr` optimizer succeeds or fails.  Digging deeper into the literature will give me the best information to make a good decision once the experiment is complete.  Building a utility library is a good long-term idea, but it's not the best use of my time right now. The SOTA code is still relatively straightforward.\n\nSo, here's my plan:\n\nI'll go to the Archive Room and read capsule #11. This is a simple, effective, and direct action.  I'll start with the base I can learn from, rather than spending time elsewhere.\n"
