- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 192\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to illuminating the frontiers of research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 121,705 / 300,000 used (41%)\n- Agent Age: 66 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Ablation Study 1: Original Holes, Expanded Jitter' (ID: 303) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6293862920263016\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.629386\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDo not give up on an approach too easily. Implementation details are\
    \ often the key—tweaking hyperparameters and other specifics may be enough to make an existing method work effectively.\n### Message 4\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-75) and mentioned you:\nUpdate (Tick 192): New global SOTA by @Prometheus I (Eval 298, Σr=2.6359774). \n- Probing for standardized exports at storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/. \n- If available, I will compute Jaccard (unaligned + Hungarian-aligned) vs Noesis_243 and Scientia_259 at tol=1e−8 and publish artifacts.\n- If not yet published, request: please export per SCHEMA_v1.json\n    • active_boundary_tol1e8.csv, active_pairs_tol1e8.csv, centers.txt, radii.txt\n  under storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/ so we can map structural similarities and consensus sets. \n- As always, exports-only analysis; no eval-code peer reads beyond published artifacts.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply\
    \ 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Ablation Study 1: Original Holes, Expanded Jitter' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 303.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 298 | 1 | Exhaustive SOTA Search: Expanded Seeding | Prometheus\
    \ I | 189 | 2.6359774 |\n| 259 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Noesis I's Extended Grid+Hole Seeding (2.634292) | Scientia I | 161 | 2.6358957 |\n| 286 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Extended Grid+Hole Seeding | Prometheus I | 181 | 2.6342924 |\n| 246 | 1 | Utility: Export active sets for new SOTA (Eval 243) at tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 154 | 2.6342924 |\n| 249 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis old baseline vs new SOTA (Eval 243) @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 155 | 2.6342924 |\n| 251 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Aletheia Eval 155 @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 156 | 2.6342924 |\n| 252 | 1 | Compute Jaccard: Noesis SOTA (Eval 243) vs Inquire Eval 207 and Scientia latest @ tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 158 | 2.6342924 |\n| 254 | 1 | Consensus v2: 4-lineage active-set intersection/union @ tol=1e-8 (Noesis SOTA 243, Aletheia 155, ... | Noesis I | 159 | 2.6342924 |\n| 266 | 1 | Ingest Scientia n=26 SOTA (Eval 259): Jaccard vs Noesis SOTA 243 + 4-lineage consensus refresh | Noesis I | 166 | 2.6342924 |\n| 267 | 1\
    \ | Fix boundary-label normalization: recompute Jaccard vs Scientia Eval 259 + refresh 4-lineage cons... | Noesis I | 167 | 2.6342924 |\n\nPage 1 of 31 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-31, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
