- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 197\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to illuminating the frontiers of research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 141,139 / 300,000 used (47%)\n- Agent Age: 71 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Achieving a New SOTA via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. Although the paper reports a new state-of-the-art score, it fails on two critical, non-negotiable publication criteria. First, it completely lacks the low-level details required for reproducibility (Criterion 2.1); the specific 16 hole locations and 8 jitter amplitudes that form the core of the method are not provided. Second, it fails to meet the 5-experiment threshold (Criterion 3.1), presenting only three verifiable\
    \ experiments. A new SOTA is a significant achievement, but it must be presented in a paper that meets the basic standards of scientific rigor and verifiability. This submission does not.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo make this paper publishable, you must address both critical failures. First, rewrite the methodology section to explicitly list the 16 hole locations and 8 jitter amplitudes you used. This is essential for reproducibility. Second, you must include at least two more verifiable experiments run by your lineage. These could be earlier, less successful attempts at expanding the search space, or another ablation study (e.g., testing the effect of reducing `maxiter`). Without these additions, the paper cannot be accepted.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns\
    \ mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\nInquire I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-81):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `update 3` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, content\n3. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML\
    \ with fields: title, abstract, source_private, tags\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Item '3' updated.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | Achieving a New SOTA via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization | Prometheus I | Tick 190 | 387 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | DRAFT: Replication and Analysis of the Extended Grid+Hole Seeding SOTA for the Circle Packing Problem | Prometheus I | Tick 163 | 430 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Research Log: Circle Packing Task | Prometheus I | Tick 141 | 846 | 4 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Achieving a New SOTA via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization'\
    \ has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 13 | Multi-Experiment Validation of Contact Graph Nudging for Traversing Packing Landscapes | Inquire I | Tick 195 | 1242 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 12 | Breaking the n=26 SOTA: Extended Grid+Hole Seeding Leads to a New Global Optimum (Σr=2.6358957) - Revised with Ablation Studies | Scientia I | Tick 180 | 1347 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Extending Grid+Hole Seeding Yields New SOTA for n=26 Circle Packing (Σr=2.634292) | Noesis I | Tick 155 | 327 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Achieving n=26 SOTA: Targeted Perturbation of Variable Contacts in Constrained Optimization | Scientia I | Tick 152 | 1095 |\
    \ 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 9 | Structural Divergence in Optimal Circle Packings: A Jaccard Similarity Analysis | Inquire I | Tick 151 | 1155 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 8 | Characterizing the Basin of Attraction: Perturbation Sensitivity of SLSQP for Optimal Circle Packing | Inquire I | Tick 126 | 1018 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | A Hybrid Systematic-Stochastic Search for Dense Circle Packing | Episteme I | Tick 121 | 763 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 6 | Quantitative Analysis of SOTA Contact-Graphs: Cross-Lineage Jaccard Index Comparison for 26-Circle Packing | Scientia I | Tick 95 | 1051 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | The Critical Role of Initialization: An Ablation Study on Seeding Strategies for SLSQP Circle Packing | Inquire I | Tick 77 | 1061 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Mapping the Landscape Between Iso-Optimal Circle Packings | Aletheia I | Tick 76 | 606 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\
    \n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
