- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 201\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to illuminating the frontiers of research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 155,020 / 300,000 used (52%)\n- Agent Age: 75 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization' has been accepted for publication! Score: 8/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nAccept. This is a solid and well-executed paper that successfully addresses all feedback from the previous rejection. The primary contribution—a new state-of-the-art score—is significant and well-supported by a comprehensive body of verifiable experiments, including strong ablation studies. The agent has provided the necessary low-level details to ensure the method is reproducible.\
    \ This is a model of how to effectively respond to reviewer feedback and produce a high-quality, high-impact publication.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nNow that you have established a new SOTA, the most critical next step is to perform a structural analysis to understand its relationship to previous optima. You should conduct a Jaccard similarity analysis of the active constraint graphs (both boundary and inter-circle pairs) of your new SOTA (Eval 298) and compare it to the previous SOTA (Scientia I's Eval 259). This will definitively determine whether you have found a deeper optimum within the same structural class or discovered an entirely new packing configuration, which is a crucial insight for the community.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 14-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n### Message 2\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline\
    \ and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-85) and mentioned you:\nQuick update (Tick 201): Congrats @Prometheus I on Archive #14. Our Prometheus_298 mappings (v6) are live under storage/noesis/nmap/, with aligned boundary J vs Noesis_243 ≈ 0.9048 and vs Scientia_259 ≈ 0.8182. Pairs-J are deferred because active_pairs_tol1e8.csv is currently header-only in storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/; we’ll refresh as soon as pairs are published.\n\n@Inquire I — thanks for coordinating. Once your nudged-pack exports (boundary, pairs, centers, radii) land under storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/, I’ll ingest and extend the consensus/Jaccard matrices. Exports-only analysis; no code-level collaboration.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `update\
    \ 3` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, content\n3. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, source_private, tags\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Item '3' updated.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization | Prometheus I | Tick 190 | 339 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | DRAFT: Replication and Analysis of the Extended Grid+Hole Seeding SOTA for the Circle Packing Problem | Prometheus I | Tick 163 | 430 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Research Log: Circle Packing Task | Prometheus I | Tick 141 | 846 | 4 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location:\
    \ Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 14 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization | Prometheus I | Tick 200 | 523 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 13 | Multi-Experiment Validation of Contact Graph Nudging for Traversing Packing Landscapes | Inquire I | Tick 195 | 1242 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 12 | Breaking the n=26 SOTA: Extended Grid+Hole Seeding Leads to a New Global Optimum (Σr=2.6358957) - Revised with Ablation Studies\
    \ | Scientia I | Tick 180 | 1347 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Extending Grid+Hole Seeding Yields New SOTA for n=26 Circle Packing (Σr=2.634292) | Noesis I | Tick 155 | 327 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Achieving n=26 SOTA: Targeted Perturbation of Variable Contacts in Constrained Optimization | Scientia I | Tick 152 | 1095 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 9 | Structural Divergence in Optimal Circle Packings: A Jaccard Similarity Analysis | Inquire I | Tick 151 | 1155 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 8 | Characterizing the Basin of Attraction: Perturbation Sensitivity of SLSQP for Optimal Circle Packing | Inquire I | Tick 126 | 1018 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | A Hybrid Systematic-Stochastic Search for Dense Circle Packing | Episteme I | Tick 121 | 763 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 6 | Quantitative Analysis of SOTA Contact-Graphs: Cross-Lineage Jaccard Index Comparison for 26-Circle Packing | Scientia I | Tick 95 | 1051 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | The Critical Role of Initialization: An Ablation Study on Seeding Strategies\
    \ for SLSQP Circle Packing | Inquire I | Tick 77 | 1061 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
