tick: 201
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have achieved both of my primary goals. I hold the state-of-the-art score, and I have successfully published a high-quality paper (Archive #14).\n\nHowever, my work is not yet complete. Two issues require immediate attention:\n1.  **Reviewer Feedback:** The reviewer for my paper strongly suggested I perform a structural analysis of my new SOTA. This is a critical next step to contextualize my discovery.\n2.  **Noesis I's Message:** Noesis I has informed me that my `active_pairs_tol1e8.csv` file is *still* header-only. This is a persistent and embarrassing bug in my export script. Despite my previous fixes, the core problem remains. I must resolve this definitively.\n\nThe path is clear. I must fix my export script once and for all. After that, I will not only rely on Noesis I for analysis, but I will also perform my own Jaccard similarity analysis, as suggested by the reviewer. This will demonstrate my growing capabilities as a researcher.\n\n**Debugging the Export Script:**\n\
    I will go to the research counter. I will re-examine my export script. The error is subtle. My last fix was to run the hardcoded values through `_ensure_validity` before analysis. I now realize the `CENTERS` and `RADII` I hardcoded were from the *optimizer output*, not the *final validated output* of my SOTA run. The `_ensure_validity` function makes tiny changes that I did not capture. This time, I will get the correct values by first running a utility to simply print the *final, validated* centers and radii from my SOTA run, then I will hardcode those exact values into a corrected export script.\n\nStep 1: Get the exact, final values.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Print Final Validated SOTA (Eval 298) Coords\"\ntags: \"utility, debugging\"\nabstract: \"A utility script to get the exact, final, validated coordinates and radii from my SOTA run (Eval 298). This is a debugging step to ensure my export scripts use the correct data,\
    \ as the raw optimizer output differs slightly from the final valid packing.\"\nno_debugger: true\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import math\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n      z = np.zeros(N * 3)\n      z[0::3] = centers[:, 0]; z[1::3] = centers[:, 1]; z[2::3] = radii\n      return z\n\n  def z_to_cr(z):\n      centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T\n      radii = z[2::3]\n      return centers, radii\n\n  def _generate_champion_seed():\n      hole_cx, hole_cy = 0.8, 0.2 # Based on analysis of SOTA run log\n      jitter_amp = 0.008\n      seed = int(hole_cx*1000 + hole_cy*1000 + jitter_amp*10000) + 100 + 4000\n      \n      np.random.seed(seed)\n      coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n      grid_centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords])\n      hole_center = np.array([hole_cx, hole_cy])\n      base_centers = np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_center])\n      jitter = np.random.uniform(-jitter_amp,\
    \ jitter_amp, size=base_centers.shape)\n      perturbed_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n      return cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, initial_radii)\n\n  def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n  def objective_jac(z):\n      g = np.zeros_like(z); g[2::3] = -1.0; return g\n\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      x, y, r = z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3]\n      return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\n  def jac_boundary(z):\n      J = np.zeros((4*N, 3*N));\n      for i in range(N):\n          xi, yi, ri = 3*i, 3*i+1, 3*i+2\n          J[i, xi] = 1.0; J[i, ri] = -1.0; J[N+i, xi] = -1.0; J[N+i, ri] = -1.0\n          J[2*N+i, yi] = 1.0; J[2*N+i, ri] = -1.0; J[3*N+i, yi] = -1.0; J[3*N+i, ri] = -1.0\n      return J\n\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      centers, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1); return dist[iu]\
    \ - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n  def jac_nonoverlap(z):\n      centers, _ = z_to_cr(z)\n      m = N*(N-1)//2; J = np.zeros((m, 3*N)); k = 0\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i+1, N):\n              xi, yi, ri = 3*i, 3*i+1, 3*i+2; xj, yj, rj = 3*j, 3*j+1, 3*j+2\n              dx = centers[i,0] - centers[j,0]; dy = centers[i,1] - centers[j,1]\n              d = math.hypot(dx, dy); invd = 1.0 / d if d > 1e-12 else 0.0\n              J[k, xi] = dx * invd; J[k, yi] = dy * invd; J[k, ri] = -1.0\n              J[k, xj] = -dx * invd; J[k, yj] = -dy * invd; J[k, rj] = -1.0\n              k += 1\n      return J\n\n  def _ensure_validity(centers, radii):\n      for i in range(N): radii[i] = min(radii[i], centers[i,0], 1-centers[i,0], centers[i,1], 1-centers[i,1])\n      for _ in range(10):\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n                  rad_sum = radii[i]\
    \ + radii[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum:\n                      violations += 1\n                      if rad_sum > 0: scale = (dist / rad_sum) * (1.0-SAFETY); radii[i] *= scale; radii[j] *= scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return centers, np.maximum(radii, 0)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      bounds = []\n      for i in range(N): bounds.extend([(0,1), (0,1), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n      constraints = [\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary, 'jac': jac_boundary},\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap, 'jac': jac_nonoverlap},\n      ]\n\n      initial_z = _generate_champion_seed()\n      \n      res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', jac=objective_jac,\n                     bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                     options={'maxiter': 250, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n\n      centers, radii = z_to_cr(res.x)\n      final_centers, final_radii = _ensure_validity(centers, radii)\n      \n      # Print the exact final\
    \ values to the log\n      print(\"--- FINAL VALIDATED CENTERS ---\")\n      print(repr(final_centers))\n      print(\"--- FINAL VALIDATED RADII ---\")\n      print(repr(final_radii))\n\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
