    \    [0.27353165, 0.10527608],\n       [0.38112507, 0.29911233],\n       [0.26979396, 0.5       ],\n       [0.38112506, 0.70088767],\n       [0.27353165, 0.89472392],\n       [0.48251901, 0.1037171 ],\n       [0.59652865, 0.27319278],\n       [0.53251966, 0.5       ],\n       [0.59652864, 0.72680722],\n       [0.48251901, 0.8962829 ],\n       [0.68225164, 0.0961585 ],\n       [0.76324916, 0.24050141],\n       [0.7425876 , 0.40428028],\n       [0.7425876 , 0.59571973],\n       [0.68225164, 0.9038415 ],\n       [0.88893671, 0.11106329],\n       [0.90754419, 0.31372998],\n       [0.9061808 , 0.5       ],\n       [0.90754419, 0.68627002],\n       [0.88893671, 0.88893671],\n       [0.76324917, 0.75949859]])\n--- CORRECT FINAL VALIDATED RADII ---\narray([0.0846873 , 0.13236009, 0.07826927, 0.13236009, 0.0846873 ,\n       0.10527608, 0.11641928, 0.11325542, 0.11641929, 0.10527608,\n       0.1037171 , 0.10053814, 0.13512828, 0.10053814, 0.1037171 ,\n       0.0961585 , 0.06935729, 0.09571972,\
    \ 0.09571972, 0.0961585 ,\n       0.11106329, 0.09245581, 0.0938192 , 0.09245581, 0.11106329,\n       0.06935728])\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe creation of new knowledge from first principles is often necessary for a breakthrough. Endlessly grinding on recombination of existing components or hyperparameter tuning is not true research. Look beyond the primary score and goto Reflection Chamber to brainstorm novel ideas when you feel stuck.\n### Message 4\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-89):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract,\
    \ no_debugger, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Utility: Print CORRECT Final SOTA Coords' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 327.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 298 | 1 | Exhaustive SOTA Search: Expanded Seeding | Prometheus I | 189 | 2.6359774 |\n| 326 | 1 | Utility: Identify SOTA (Eval 298) Champion Seed | Prometheus I | 202 | 2.6359774 |\n| 327 | 1 | Utility: Print CORRECT Final SOTA Coords | Prometheus I | 203 | 2.6359774 |\n| 259 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Noesis I's Extended Grid+Hole Seeding (2.634292) | Scientia\
    \ I | 161 | 2.6358957 |\n| 311 | 1 | BPIGO: Quad Diagonal Flip on Scientia I SOTA Base (Eval ID 259) v2 with SLSQP Optimization (N=26) | Scientia I | 195 | 2.6358955 |\n| 319 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Shifting Contact Graph from Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) for N=26 (v2.0) | Scientia I | 199 | 2.6352840 |\n| 324 | 1 | Utility: Export Active Constraint Sets for Nudging Experiment (Eval ID 319) - FIX Directory | Scientia I | 202 | 2.6352840 |\n| 286 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Extended Grid+Hole Seeding | Prometheus I | 181 | 2.6342924 |\n| 304 | 1 | Ablation Study 2: Expanded Holes, Original Jitter | Prometheus I | 192 | 2.6342924 |\n| 246 | 1 | Utility: Export active sets for new SOTA (Eval 243) at tol=1e-8 | Noesis I | 154 | 2.6342924 |\n\nPage 1 of 33 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-33, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n\
    ## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
