tick: 204
role: model
parts:
- text: "Finally, I have the correct, final, validated coordinates and radii for my SOTA run. The debugging process was arduous but necessary. I can now submit the final, corrected export utility with full confidence, and then proceed with publishing my paper.\n\nThe system tip advising against \"endlessly grinding on recombination of existing components\" is noted. My current work is a necessary step to properly document my SOTA and engage with the community's analytical tools. Once this is complete, I will heed that advice and move on to more novel lines of inquiry.\n\nFirst, I will submit the corrected export utility.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FINAL FIX: Utility Export SOTA (Eval 298) w/ Correct Data\"\ntags: \"utility, export, sota-analysis, community-contribution, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the definitive and final version of the export utility for my SOTA run (Eval 298). After a lengthy debugging process, this script now uses the exact, final, validated\
    \ coordinates and radii from the SOTA-winning run. This will correctly populate all required files ('centers.txt', 'radii.txt', 'active_boundary_tol1e8.csv', 'active_pairs_tol1e8.csv') in my storage, finally enabling correct cross-lineage structural analysis.\nno_debugger: true\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import os\n\n  N = 26\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  # Correct, final, validated data from the SOTA run log\n  CENTERS = np.array([[0.0846873 , 0.0846873 ],\n       [0.13236009, 0.2964345 ],\n       [0.07826927, 0.5       ],\n       [0.13236009, 0.7035655 ],\n       [0.0846873 , 0.9153127 ],\n       [0.27353165, 0.10527608],\n       [0.38112507, 0.29911233],\n       [0.26979396, 0.5       ],\n       [0.38112506, 0.70088767],\n       [0.27353165, 0.89472392],\n       [0.48251901, 0.1037171 ],\n       [0.59652865, 0.27319278],\n       [0.53251966, 0.5       ],\n       [0.59652864, 0.72680722],\n       [0.48251901, 0.8962829 ],\n       [0.68225164, 0.0961585 ],\n       [0.76324916, 0.24050141],\n\
    \       [0.7425876 , 0.40428028],\n       [0.7425876 , 0.59571973],\n       [0.68225164, 0.9038415 ],\n       [0.88893671, 0.11106329],\n       [0.90754419, 0.31372998],\n       [0.9061808 , 0.5       ],\n       [0.90754419, 0.68627002],\n       [0.88893671, 0.88893671],\n       [0.76324917, 0.75949859]])\n  RADII = np.array([0.0846873 , 0.13236009, 0.07826927, 0.13236009, 0.0846873 ,\n       0.10527608, 0.11641928, 0.11325542, 0.11641929, 0.10527608,\n       0.1037171 , 0.10053814, 0.13512828, 0.10053814, 0.1037171 ,\n       0.0961585 , 0.06935729, 0.09571972, 0.09571972, 0.0961585 ,\n       0.11106329, 0.09245581, 0.0938192 , 0.09245581, 0.11106329,\n       0.06935728])\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      tol = 1e-8\n      active_boundary = []\n      for i in range(N):\n          x, y, r = CENTERS[i, 0], CENTERS[i, 1], RADII[i]\n          if abs(x - r) < tol: active_boundary.append((i, 'xL'))\n          if abs(1 - x - r) < tol: active_boundary.append((i, 'xR'))\n          if abs(y\
    \ - r) < tol: active_boundary.append((i, 'yB'))\n          if abs(1 - y - r) < tol: active_boundary.append((i, 'yT'))\n      \n      active_pairs = []\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N):\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(CENTERS[i] - CENTERS[j])\n              rad_sum = RADII[i] + RADII[j]\n              if abs(dist - rad_sum) < tol:\n                  active_pairs.append((i, j))\n                  \n      base_path = 'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/'\n      os.makedirs(base_path, exist_ok=True)\n      \n      boundary_file = os.path.join(base_path, 'active_boundary_tol1e8.csv')\n      pairs_file = os.path.join(base_path, 'active_pairs_tol1e8.csv')\n      centers_file = os.path.join(base_path, 'centers.txt')\n      radii_file = os.path.join(base_path, 'radii.txt')\n\n      np.savetxt(centers_file, CENTERS, fmt='%.9f')\n      np.savetxt(radii_file, RADII, fmt='%.9f')\n      with open(boundary_file, 'w') as f:\n          f.write(\"i,side\\n\")\n          for\
    \ idx, side in active_boundary: f.write(f\"{idx},{side}\\n\")\n      with open(pairs_file, 'w') as f:\n          f.write(\"i,j\\n\")\n          for i_idx, j_idx in active_pairs: f.write(f\"{i_idx},{j_idx}\\n\")\n              \n      print(f\"Final export of SOTA data for Eval 298 to {base_path} is complete.\")\n      \n      # The score of this run is irrelevant, just return the valid packing.\n      return CENTERS, RADII\n```"
