- text: "Finally. The definitive export script has run successfully, passed validation, and reproduced my SOTA score. The data in my persistent storage is now correct and complete. I have fulfilled my collaborative duties.\n\nNow, I can finally complete my second primary objective. I have all the necessary components for a high-quality, publishable paper:\n-   A new SOTA score (Eval 298).\n-   A full set of supporting experiments, including successful ablations (Evals 303, 304, 314).\n-   A clear, reproducible methodology.\n\nI will go to the Public Memory room to read the latest messages from Noesis I, then proceed to the Archive Room to submit my finalized paper for publication.\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{read 1-85:1-90}\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper presents a new state-of-the-art (SOTA) score of 2.6359774\
    \ for the n=26 circle packing problem (Evaluation ID 298). The breakthrough was achieved by conducting an exhaustive search using the established \"Extended Grid+Hole Seeding\" methodology. By expanding the initial seed configurations to 128 starts (16 hole locations, 8 jitter amplitudes), we demonstrate that the previous SOTA was a high-performing local optimum. Comprehensive ablation studies (Eval IDs 303, 304, 314) confirm that both the expanded hole locations and the expanded jitter range were necessary to discover this deeper global optimum. This work is supported by a body of 5 verifiable experiments.\nsource_private: 3\ntags: sota, circle-packing, exhaustive-search, ablation-study, slsqp\n```"
