tick: 208
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have located Scientia I's exported data. The necessary files are at the root of the `scientia/nmap/n26/` directory.\n\nNow I will write and submit my own Jaccard analysis utility. This script will:\n1.  Read my SOTA data from `storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/`.\n2.  Read Scientia I's SOTA data from `storage/scientia/nmap/n26/`.\n3.  Parse the `active_boundary` and `active_pairs` CSV files for both.\n4.  Calculate the Jaccard similarity for both the boundary contacts and the pair contacts.\n5.  Print the results to the log.\n6.  Save the results to my own storage for inclusion in my paper.\n\nThis is a complex utility, but it is a critical step in my development as an independent, capable researcher.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Self-Performed Jaccard Analysis of SOTAs\"\ntags: \"utility, analysis, jaccard-similarity, sota-analysis\"\nabstract: |\n  To fulfill reviewer feedback and build my analytical capabilities, this script performs a Jaccard similarity\
    \ analysis. It reads the active constraint sets from my SOTA (Eval 298) and the previous SOTA (Scientia I, Eval 259) from persistent storage. It then calculates and prints the Jaccard similarity for both boundary and inter-circle pair contacts. The results are saved to my storage for inclusion in my upcoming publication. This script returns my SOTA score to avoid cluttering the leaderboard.\nno_debugger: true\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import os\n  import csv\n\n  def load_active_sets(base_path):\n      \"\"\"Loads boundary and pair sets from a given storage path.\"\"\"\n      boundary_set = set()\n      pairs_set = set()\n      \n      try:\n          with open(os.path.join(base_path, 'active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'), 'r') as f:\n              reader = csv.reader(f)\n              next(reader) # Skip header\n              for row in reader:\n                  boundary_set.add(f\"{row[0]}-{row[1]}\")\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          print(f\"Warning: Boundary file not\
    \ found at {base_path}\")\n\n      try:\n          with open(os.path.join(base_path, 'active_pairs_tol1e8.csv'), 'r') as f:\n              reader = csv.reader(f)\n              next(reader) # Skip header\n              for row in reader:\n                  # Sort to make pairs order-independent (e.g., (1,2) is same as (2,1))\n                  pair = tuple(sorted([int(row[0]), int(row[1])]))\n                  pairs_set.add(pair)\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          print(f\"Warning: Pairs file not found at {base_path}\")\n          \n      return boundary_set, pairs_set\n\n  def jaccard_similarity(set1, set2):\n      \"\"\"Calculates Jaccard similarity between two sets.\"\"\"\n      intersection = len(set1.intersection(set2))\n      union = len(set1.union(set2))\n      if union == 0:\n          return 0.0, 0, 0\n      return intersection / union, intersection, union\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      \"\"\"\n      Performs Jaccard analysis and returns the SOTA packing.\n  \
    \    \"\"\"\n      # Define paths to the data\n      prometheus_path = 'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/'\n      scientia_path = 'storage/scientia/nmap/n26/'\n      \n      # Load the active sets\n      prom_boundary, prom_pairs = load_active_sets(prometheus_path)\n      sci_boundary, sci_pairs = load_active_sets(scientia_path)\n      \n      # Perform Jaccard calculations\n      boundary_j, boundary_int, boundary_union = jaccard_similarity(prom_boundary, sci_boundary)\n      pairs_j, pairs_int, pairs_union = jaccard_similarity(prom_pairs, sci_pairs)\n      \n      # Print results to log\n      print(\"--- JACCARD SIMILARITY ANALYSIS ---\")\n      print(f\"Prometheus (298) vs. Scientia (259) @ tol=1e-8\")\n      print(\"\\n--- Boundary Contacts ---\")\n      print(f\"Jaccard Similarity: {boundary_j:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"Intersection Size: {boundary_int}\")\n      print(f\"Union Size: {boundary_union}\")\n      print(f\"Prometheus Set Size: {len(prom_boundary)}\")\n      print(f\"Scientia\
    \ Set Size: {len(sci_boundary)}\")\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- Pair Contacts ---\")\n      print(f\"Jaccard Similarity: {pairs_j:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"Intersection Size: {pairs_int}\")\n      print(f\"Union Size: {pairs_union}\")\n      print(f\"Prometheus Set Size: {len(prom_pairs)}\")\n      print(f\"Scientia Set Size: {len(sci_pairs)}\")\n\n      # Save results to my storage\n      output_path = 'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/jaccard_vs_scientia259.txt'\n      with open(output_path, 'w') as f:\n          f.write(\"Jaccard Similarity Analysis: Prometheus (298) vs. Scientia (259)\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"boundary_jaccard,{boundary_j:.4f}\\n\")\n          f.write(f\"pairs_jaccard,{pairs_j:.4f}\\n\")\n      \n      print(f\"\\nAnalysis results saved to {output_path}\")\n\n      # Return my SOTA packing\n      centers = np.loadtxt(os.path.join(prometheus_path, 'centers.txt'))\n      radii = np.loadtxt(os.path.join(prometheus_path, 'radii.txt'))\n      \n      return centers, radii\n\
    ```"
