tick: 211
role: model
parts:
- text: "My paper is now fully updated with the crucial structural analysis data. I am ready to publish as soon as my cooldown ends.\n\nWhile I wait, I will begin my exploration of the \"nudging\" technique. This is the clear research frontier, and I must not fall behind. My goal is to replicate Inquire I's work to understand the methodology and then attempt to apply it in a novel way.\n\nI will start by creating an experiment that attempts to \"nudge\" my own SOTA packing. I'll choose a pair of circles that are *not* in contact in my SOTA and encourage them to touch, while discouraging a pair that *are* in contact. This will serve as my first hands-on experience with this new, promising technique.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Nudging Experiment 1: Modifying Prometheus SOTA\"\ntags: \"nudging, innovation, contact-graph, landscape-exploration\"\nabstract: |\n  This is my first experiment with the 'nudging' methodology pioneered by Inquire\
    \ I. Starting from my own SOTA packing (Eval 298), I will apply a penalized objective function to modify its contact graph. I will encourage a new contact between a non-touching pair of circles while simultaneously discouraging an existing contact. This experiment serves as a replication of the nudging technique and a first step towards using it for novel landscape exploration.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import math\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  # My SOTA packing from Eval 298\n  SOTA_CENTERS = np.array([[0.0846873 , 0.0846873 ], [0.13236009, 0.2964345 ], [0.07826927, 0.5], [0.13236009, 0.7035655 ], [0.0846873 , 0.9153127 ], [0.27353165, 0.10527608], [0.38112507, 0.29911233], [0.26979396, 0.5], [0.38112506, 0.70088767], [0.27353165, 0.89472392], [0.48251901, 0.1037171 ], [0.59652865, 0.27319278], [0.53251966, 0.5], [0.59652864, 0.72680722], [0.48251901, 0.8962829 ], [0.68225164, 0.0961585 ], [0.76324916, 0.24050141],\
    \ [0.7425876 , 0.40428028], [0.7425876 , 0.59571973], [0.68225164, 0.9038415 ], [0.88893671, 0.11106329], [0.90754419, 0.31372998], [0.9061808 , 0.5], [0.90754419, 0.68627002], [0.88893671, 0.88893671], [0.76324917, 0.75949859]])\n  SOTA_RADII = np.array([0.0846873 , 0.13236009, 0.07826927, 0.13236009, 0.0846873 , 0.10527608, 0.11641928, 0.11325542, 0.11641929, 0.10527608, 0.1037171 , 0.10053814, 0.13512828, 0.10053814, 0.1037171 , 0.0961585 , 0.06935729, 0.09571972, 0.09571972, 0.0961585 , 0.11106329, 0.09245581, 0.0938192 , 0.09245581, 0.11106329, 0.06935728])\n\n  def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n      z = np.zeros(N * 3)\n      z[0::3] = centers[:, 0]; z[1::3] = centers[:, 1]; z[2::3] = radii\n      return z\n\n  def z_to_cr(z):\n      centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T\n      radii = z[2::3]\n      return centers, radii\n\n  # --- Nudging Objective Function ---\n  def objective(z, encourage_pair, discourage_pair):\n      base_obj = -np.sum(z[2::3])\n      centers, radii = z_to_cr(z)\n\
    \      \n      alpha = 100 # Encourage penalty\n      beta = 100  # Discourage penalty\n      eps_close = 1e-8\n      eps_far = 0.005\n\n      # Encourage Term\n      i, j = encourage_pair\n      dist_ij = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n      encourage_penalty = alpha * max(0, dist_ij - (radii[i] + radii[j] + eps_close))**2\n      \n      # Discourage Term\n      k, l = discourage_pair\n      dist_kl = np.linalg.norm(centers[k] - centers[l])\n      discourage_penalty = beta * max(0, (radii[k] + radii[l] + eps_far) - dist_kl)**2\n      \n      return base_obj + encourage_penalty + discourage_penalty\n\n  def jac_boundary(z):\n      # Code for jacobians omitted for brevity, but would be included in a real run\n      pass\n  def jac_nonoverlap(z):\n      pass\n\n  def _ensure_validity(centers, radii):\n      # Ensure validity function as used in previous submissions\n      for i in range(N): radii[i] = min(radii[i], centers[i,0], 1-centers[i,0], centers[i,1], 1-centers[i,1])\n\
    \      for _ in range(20):\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum:\n                      violations += 1\n                      if rad_sum > 0: scale = (dist / rad_sum) * (1.0-SAFETY); radii[i] *= scale; radii[j] *= scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return centers, np.maximum(radii, 0)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # From analysis of SOTA contacts, (0, 5) is an existing contact.\n      # (0, 1) is not a contact. Let's try to swap them.\n      encourage_pair = (0, 1)\n      discourage_pair = (0, 5)\n\n      initial_z = cr_to_z(SOTA_CENTERS, SOTA_RADII)\n      \n      # Using numerical approximation for Jacobian of the complex objective\n      # Constraints are the same as before, but not showing full code for brevity\n      bounds = []\n      for\
    \ i in range(N): bounds.extend([(0,1), (0,1), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n      constraints = [\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda z: np.concatenate([z[0::3]-z[2::3], 1-z[0::3]-z[2::3], z[1::3]-z[2::3], 1-z[1::3]-z[2::3]])},\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda z: np.array([np.linalg.norm(z_to_cr(z)[0][i] - z_to_cr(z)[0][j]) - (z_to_cr(z)[1][i] + z_to_cr(z)[1][j]) for i in range(N) for j in range(i + 1, N)])}\n      ]\n      \n      res = minimize(objective, initial_z, args=(encourage_pair, discourage_pair), method='SLSQP',\n                     jac='2-point', # Approximate jacobian for the penalized objective\n                     bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                     options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n      \n      centers, radii = z_to_cr(res.x)\n      final_centers, final_radii = _ensure_validity(centers, radii)\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
