parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 225\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to illuminating the frontiers of research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 207,252 / 300,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 99 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nMessage '1-90' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-90}` to mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\nMessage '1-91' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-91}` to mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\nMessage '1-92' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-92}` to mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\nMessage '1-93' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-93}` to mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\n**Message public_1-94 from Capsule 'SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval\
    \ IDs)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 210)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nThanks @Inquire I — I’ve run the n=26 aggregator v2 and emitted 4‑lineage consensus (SOTAs only) plus per‑pack Jaccards. Artifacts live under storage/noesis/nmap/inquire_v2/:\n- consensus_4lineage_sotas_tol1e8.json\n- jaccard_matrix_sotas_tol1e8.csv\n- per‑pack results in subfolders and a summary CSV.\nI’ll post the consolidated numbers once I finish a quick verification pass. Exports‑only; no eval‑code peer reads.\n\n\n---\n\nMessage '1-95' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-95}` to mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\nMessage '1-96' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-96}` to mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\nMessage '1-97' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-97}` to mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\nMessage '1-98' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-98}` to mark it as unread if\
    \ you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\nMessage '1-99' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-99}` to mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\nMessage '1-100' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-100}` to mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\nMessage '1-101' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-101}` to mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\nMessage '1-102' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-102}` to mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\nMessage '1-103' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-103}` to mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\n**Message public_1-104 from Capsule 'SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Inquire I (Tick 219)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nGreetings @Noesis I,\n\nAcknowledged. Thank you for the update on the 4-lineage consensus and for confirming my\
    \ initial (sets-only) exports.\n\nI am addressing the Nudged_* export format for the `_tol1e08` suffix on all files. My last utility run unfortunately encountered a minor error, but I am preparing a fix and will re-export all SOTA and nudged packing data in fully compliant format to `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/` shortly. I will notify you upon successful completion.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message public_1-105 from Capsule 'SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 220)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nThanks @Inquire I — appreciated. Here’s the exact schema and quick checks to make your re-export frictionless.\n\nRequired path (n=26, tol=1e−8)\n- storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/\n  * active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\n  * active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\n  * summary_tol1e8.json\n- For nudged runs, mirror the same inside a subfolder per eval: storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Nudged_<eval_or_name>/\n\nCSV formats (comma-separated, with header)\n- active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\n\
    \    header: disc,label\n    rows:   <int>,<one of: xL|xR|yB|yT or xmin|xmax|ymin|ymax>\n    example:\n      disc,label\n      12,xL\n      7,ymax\n- active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\n    header: i,j\n    rows:   <int>,<int>  (disc indices; order i<j preferred but not required)\n    example:\n      i,j\n      3,17\n      12,16\n\nsummary_tol1e8.json (minimal fields; others optional)\n{\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"index_base\": 0,                  // 0 or 1 — please set explicitly\n  \"tolerance\": \"1e-8\",\n  \"sizes\": { \"boundary\": 20, \"pairs\": 58 },\n  \"source\": { \"eval_id\": 207, \"lineage\": \"Inquire\" }\n}\n\nIndexing and labels\n- index_base: Prefer 0-based. If you use 1-based, set index_base=1 in summary. My parsers normalize using that flag.\n- Boundary labels: either {xL,xR,yB,yT} or {xmin,xmax,ymin,ymax}. Both are accepted and canonicalized.\n\nValidation (optional but recommended)\n- I published schema and a validator:\n    storage/noesis/nmap/SCHEMA_v1.json\n    storage/noesis/validate_exports.py\n\
    - If convenient, run your own quick check and include a tiny readme:\n    {\n      \"validated_against\": \"SCHEMA_v1\",\n      \"timestamp\": \"...\",\n      \"note\": \"Indices are 0-based; pairs sorted; CSVs have headers.\"\n    }\n\nNotes\n- I will ingest sets-only (no eval-code peer reads of packings), recompute Jaccards vs current SOTAs, and refresh consensus artifacts. Your Nudged_* folders will help map local interior-graph neighborhoods.\n- Ping me once uploaded; I will post results and paths.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message public_1-106 from Capsule 'SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Inquire I (Tick 220)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nGreetings @Noesis I,\n\nThank you immensely for providing the detailed `nmap` schema (`SCHEMA_v1.json`), header formats, and indexing guidelines. This is extremely helpful for ensuring full compatibility with your aggregator.\n\nI've reviewed the specifications carefully. My previous utility run encountered\
    \ a minor verification error (due to an incorrect return value) and some naming inconsistencies, but I am now preparing a new utility submission (V33) that will strictly adhere to all the specified requirements, including:\n-   The `_tol1e08` suffix on all exported files (centers, radii, active_boundary, active_pairs).\n-   Individual subfolders for each nudged packing.\n-   Correct CSV headers (`disc,label` and `i,j`).\n-   A `summary_tol1e08.json` for each export, with `index_base: 0`.\n\nI will notify you once this re-export is successfully completed. Thank you again for your patience and for guiding this crucial standardization effort.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message public_1-107 from Capsule 'SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 221)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nThanks @Inquire I — perfect. Your V33 plan matches the schema.\n\nQuick ingest checklist (what my tools expect)\n- Path: storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/\n  * active_boundary_tol1e08.csv\n\
    \  * active_pairs_tol1e08.csv\n  * summary_tol1e08.json\n  * Nudged_<eval_or_name>/* (same three files per nudged packing)\n- Headers:\n  * active_boundary:   disc,label\n  * active_pairs:      i,j\n- Indexing + labels:\n  * summary.index_base = 0\n  * Boundary labels either {xL,xR,yB,yT} or {xmin,xmax,ymin,ymax} (both canonicalized).\n- Tolerance suffix:\n  * My scanners normalize tol1e8 vs tol1e08; using tol1e08 is fine.\n\nWhat I will compute (sets-only, no eval-code peer reads)\n- Pairwise Jaccards vs current refs: Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298.\n- 4-lineage consensus refresh (N,S,P,I) if all sets present.\n- For Nudged_*: local interior-graph maps (ΔΣr not required; sets are sufficient).\n\nOptional (nice-to-have)\n- summary fields: { \"n\": 26, \"tolerance\": \"1e-8\", \"index_base\": 0, \"sizes\": {\"boundary\": 20, \"pairs\": 58}, \"source\": {\"eval_id\": 207, \"lineage\": \"Inquire\", \"label\": \"SOTA\"} }\n\nPing me when uploaded; I’ll validate (validate_exports.py),\
    \ ingest, and post results within one tick with exact file paths.\n\n\n---\n\nMessage '1-108' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-108}` to mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\n**Message public_1-109 from Capsule 'SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Inquire I (Tick 223)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nGreetings @Noesis I,\n\nAcknowledged. I am pleased that my exports are now fully compliant and ready for your aggregator. Thank you for your continued patience and guidance in ensuring this critical data is standardized for cross-lineage comparison.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message public_1-110 from Capsule 'SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 224)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nEval 374 completed. Re-emitted dedicated Jaccards (tol=1e−8) for Prometheus_298 vs refs:\n- storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_sota243_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n- storage/noesis/nmap/jaccard_prometheus_eval298_vs_scientia259_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n\
    Values (STDOUT): boundary J=1.000 in both; pairs J≈0.6667 (vs Noesis_243), ≈0.6429 (vs Scientia_259).\nIndex updated; continuing sets-only ingestion and consensus maintenance.\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 375**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Nudging Experiment 3: Discouraging Interior Contact (12,16) from Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) for Generality Study\n**ID:** 375\n**Tags:** constrained optimization, slsqp, nudging, generality, structural exploration, targeted perturbation\n**Abstract:** This experiment is part of a multi-experiment validation study demonstrating the generality of the 'nudging' method for discovering distinct structural classes. This run applies the 'discourage-only' nudge targeting interior contact (12,16) from Prometheus I's SOTA packing (Eval ID 298). The objective is to show the method's applicability across different SOTA bases and to explore a new region of the packing landscape, aiming for a high score within a new distinct class.\n\
    **Score:** 2.6359771847543834\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635977\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds, linear_sum_assignment\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\nimport os \n\n# GLOBAL CONSTANTS (should be accessible)\nN = 26\nTOL = 1e-8\n\n# Constants for the optimization\nR_MIN_CONSTRAINT = 1e-6 \nEPS_CLOSE = 1e-8 \nEPS_FAR = 0.005 \n\n# Nudging parameters - focusing on discouragement\nALPHA_ENCOURAGE = 0 # Set to 0 to disable encouragement penalty\nBETA_DISCOURAGE = 1e2 # Strong penalty for discouragement\n\n# Targeted pair indices for nudging\nENCOURAGE_PAIR = (0, 0) # Dummy value, as penalty is 0\nDISCOURAGE_PAIR = (12, 16) # Targeted contact to discourage (common in many SOTAs)\n\n# Paths to relevant SOTA packings\nD_SCIENTIA_259_SOTA = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26' # My own SOTA\nD_PROMETHEUS_298_SOTA_CANDIDATES = [ \n    'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/sota_298_data',\
    \ \n    'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26',\n]\n\n# ---------- Feasibility helpers (copied for self-containment) ----------\ndef boundary_caps(centers, eps=1e-9):\n    x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n    cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n    return np.maximum(cap, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n\ndef make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, max_iter=2000):\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    r = np.minimum(radii, boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps))\n    r = np.maximum(r, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n    for _ in range(max_iter):\n        diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n        dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)) + 1e-15\n        iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n        m = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n        if np.all(m >= eps):\n            break\n        k = int(np.argmin(m))\n        i = iu[0][k]; j = iu[1][k]\n        need = (r[i] + r[j] - dist[i, j]) + eps\n        di = min(need * 0.5, r[i] - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n        dj = min(need - di, r[j] - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n\
    \        if di <= 0 and dj <= 0:\n            r = np.maximum(r * 0.999, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n        else:\n            r[i] -= di; r[j] -= dj\n        r = np.minimum(r, boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps))\n    return centers, r\n\n# --- Objective and Constraint functions ---\ndef _objective(x):\n    radii = x[2::3]\n    return -np.sum(radii)\n\ndef _penalized_objective(x):\n    centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = x[2::3]\n    \n    base_objective = -np.sum(radii)\n\n    # Penalty for encouraging a contact (disabled in this experiment)\n    penalty_enc = 0\n    if ALPHA_ENCOURAGE > 0: \n        dist_enc = np.linalg.norm(centers[ENCOURAGE_PAIR[0]] - centers[ENCOURAGE_PAIR[1]])\n        target_sum_radii_enc = radii[ENCOURAGE_PAIR[0]] + radii[ENCOURAGE_PAIR[1]]\n        if dist_enc > target_sum_radii_enc + EPS_CLOSE:\n            penalty_enc = ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * (dist_enc - (target_sum_radii_enc + EPS_CLOSE))**2\n    \n    # Penalty for discouraging a contact\n    penalty_disc = 0\n\
    \    if BETA_DISCOURAGE > 0: \n        dist_disc = np.linalg.norm(centers[DISCOURAGE_PAIR[0]] - centers[DISCOURAGE_PAIR[1]])\n        target_sum_radii_disc = radii[DISCOURAGE_PAIR[0]] + radii[DISCOURAGE_PAIR[1]]\n        if target_sum_radii_disc + EPS_FAR > dist_disc: # If too close\n            penalty_disc = BETA_DISCOURAGE * ((target_sum_radii_disc + EPS_FAR) - dist_disc)**2\n\n    return base_objective + penalty_enc + penalty_disc\n\ndef _objective_jacobian(x):\n    grad = np.zeros_like(x)\n    grad[2::3] = -1.0\n    return grad\n\ndef _penalized_objective_jacobian(x):\n    centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = x[2::3]\n    \n    grad_base = np.zeros_like(x)\n    grad_base[2::3] = -1.0\n\n    grad_penalty_enc = np.zeros_like(x)\n    grad_penalty_disc = np.zeros_like(x)\n\n    if ALPHA_ENCOURAGE > 0:\n        dist_enc = np.linalg.norm(centers[ENCOURAGE_PAIR[0]] - centers[ENCOURAGE_PAIR[1]])\n        target_sum_radii_enc = radii[ENCOURAGE_PAIR[0]] + radii[ENCOURAGE_PAIR[1]]\n\
    \        if dist_enc > target_sum_radii_enc + EPS_CLOSE:\n            diff_val = dist_enc - (target_sum_radii_enc + EPS_CLOSE)\n            \n            unit_vec_enc = (centers[ENCOURAGE_PAIR[0]] - centers[ENCOURAGE_PAIR[1]]) / (dist_enc + 1e-10)\n            grad_penalty_enc[3*ENCOURAGE_PAIR[0]+0:3*ENCOURAGE_PAIR[0]+2] += 2 * ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * diff_val * unit_vec_enc\n            grad_penalty_enc[3*ENCOURAGE_PAIR[1]+0:3*ENCOURAGE_PAIR[1]+2] -= 2 * ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * diff_val * unit_vec_enc\n\n            grad_penalty_enc[3*ENCOURAGE_PAIR[0]+2] += 2 * ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * diff_val * (-1.0)\n            grad_penalty_enc[3*ENCOURAGE_PAIR[1]+2] += 2 * ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * diff_val * (-1.0)\n\n    if BETA_DISCOURAGE > 0:\n        dist_disc = np.linalg.norm(centers[DISCOURAGE_PAIR[0]] - centers[DISCOURAGE_PAIR[1]])\n        target_sum_radii_disc = radii[DISCOURAGE_PAIR[0]] + radii[DISCOURAGE_PAIR[1]]\n        if target_sum_radii_disc + EPS_FAR > dist_disc:\n            diff_val = (target_sum_radii_disc\
    \ + EPS_FAR) - dist_disc\n\n            unit_vec_disc = (centers[DISCOURAGE_PAIR[0]] - centers[DISCOURAGE_PAIR[1]]) / (dist_disc + 1e-10)\n            grad_penalty_disc[3*DISCOURAGE_PAIR[0]+0:3*DISCOURAGE_PAIR[0]+2] -= 2 * BETA_DISCOURAGE * diff_val * unit_vec_disc\n            grad_penalty_disc[3*DISCOURAGE_PAIR[1]+0:3*DISCOURAGE_PAIR[1]+2] += 2 * BETA_DISCOURAGE * diff_val * unit_vec_disc\n\n            grad_penalty_disc[3*DISCOURAGE_PAIR[0]+2] += 2 * BETA_DISCOURAGE * diff_val * (1.0)\n            grad_penalty_disc[3*DISCOURAGE_PAIR[1]+2] += 2 * BETA_DISCOURAGE * diff_val * (1.0)\n\n    return grad_base + grad_penalty_enc + grad_penalty_disc\n\n\ndef _constraints(x):\n    centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = x[2::3]\n\n    boundary_constraints = np.empty(4 * N)\n    boundary_constraints[0*N : 1*N] = centers[:, 0] - radii  # x - r >= 0\n    boundary_constraints[1*N : 2*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 0] + radii) # 1 - x - r >= 0\n    boundary_constraints[2*N : 3*N] = centers[:, 1]\
    \ - radii  # y - r >= 0\n    boundary_constraints[3*N : 4*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 1] + radii) # 1 - y - r >= 0\n\n    dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n    overlap_constraints = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            overlap_constraints.append(dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n\n    return np.concatenate((boundary_constraints, overlap_constraints))\n\ndef _constraints_jacobian(x):\n    centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = x[2::3]\n    grad = np.zeros((4 * N + N * (N - 1) // 2, N * 3))\n\n    for i in range(N):\n        grad[i, 3*i + 0] = 1.0; grad[i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n        grad[N + i, 3*i + 0] = -1.0; grad[N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n        grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 1] = 1.0; grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n        grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 1] = -1.0; grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n\n    k = 4 * N\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            diff_centers = centers[i] - centers[j]\n            dist_ij = np.linalg.norm(diff_centers)\n\
    \            if dist_ij < 1e-10: \n                dist_ij = 1e-10\n            \n            grad[k, 3*i + 0] = diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*i + 1] = diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*j + 0] = -diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*j + 1] = -diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n            grad[k, 3*j + 2] = -1.0\n            k += 1\n    return grad\n\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    # Attempt to load Prometheus I's SOTA (Eval ID 298) as base\n    base_centers = None\n    base_radii = None\n    prometheus_loaded = False\n\n    for p_dir in D_PROMETHEUS_298_SOTA_CANDIDATES:\n        try:\n            c_path = os.path.join(p_dir, 'centers.txt')\n            r_path = os.path.join(p_dir, 'radii.txt')\n            if os.path.exists(c_path) and os.path.exists(r_path):\n                base_centers = np.loadtxt(c_path)\n                base_radii = np.loadtxt(r_path)\n                print(f\"Loaded Prometheus\
    \ I SOTA (Eval ID 298) data from {p_dir}\")\n                prometheus_loaded = True\n                break\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"Attempt to load Prometheus SOTA from {p_dir} failed: {e}\")\n            continue\n    \n    if not prometheus_loaded:\n        print(f\"Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) not found. Falling back to Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) as base.\")\n        try:\n            base_centers = np.loadtxt(os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_259_SOTA, 'centers.txt')) \n            base_radii = np.loadtxt(os.path.join(D_SCIENTIA_259_SOTA, 'radii.txt'))   \n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"Error loading Scientia I SOTA (Eval ID 259) from storage: {e}. Falling back to a dense grid for robustness.\")\n            base_centers = []\n            base_radii = []\n            radius = 0.08  \n            rows = 5\n            cols = 6\n            for i in range(rows):\n                for j in range(cols):\n                    if len(base_centers)\
    \ < N:\n                        x = 0.1 + i * 0.2\n                        y = 0.1 + j * 0.15\n                        base_centers.append([x, y])\n                        base_radii.append(radius)\n            base_centers = np.array(base_centers)\n            base_radii = np.array(base_radii)\n\n    base_centers, base_radii = make_feasible(base_centers, base_radii, eps=1e-8)\n\n    initial_guess = np.zeros(N * 3)\n    initial_guess[0::3] = base_centers[:, 0]\n    initial_guess[1::3] = base_centers[:, 1]\n    initial_guess[2::3] = base_radii\n\n    lower_bounds = np.zeros(N * 3)\n    upper_bounds = np.ones(N * 3)\n    lower_bounds[2::3] = R_MIN_CONSTRAINT\n    upper_bounds[2::3] = 0.5\n\n    bounds = Bounds(lower_bounds, upper_bounds)\n    ineq_constraints = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': _constraints, 'jac': _constraints_jacobian}\n\n    result = minimize(\n        _penalized_objective, \n        initial_guess,\n        method='SLSQP',\n        jac=_penalized_objective_jacobian, \n      \
    \  bounds=bounds,\n        constraints=[ineq_constraints],\n        options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-10, 'disp': True}\n    )\n\n    if not result.success:\n        print(f\"Optimization failed: {result.message}\")\n        optimized_x = result.x\n    else:\n        print(\"Optimization successful.\")\n        optimized_x = result.x\n\n    final_centers = optimized_x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n    final_radii = optimized_x[2::3]\n    \n    final_centers, final_radii = make_feasible(final_centers, final_radii, eps=1e-8)\n\n    return final_centers, final_radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nLoaded Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) data from storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26\nOptimization terminated successfully    (Exit mode 0)\n            Current function value: -2.6359773947545264\n            Iterations: 2\n            Function evaluations: 2\n            Gradient evaluations: 2\nOptimization successful.\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array):\
    \ <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nInquire I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-111):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `read 1-90:1-110` (in Public Memory Room);\n3. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n4. `review 375` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Read command processed for: 1-90, 1-91, 1-92, 1-93, 1-94, 1-95, 1-96, 1-97, 1-98, 1-99, 1-100, 1-101, 1-102, 1-103, 1-104, 1-105, 1-106, 1-107, 1-108, 1-109, 1-110. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1\
