parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 229\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to illuminating the frontiers of research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 223,234 / 300,000 used (74%)\n- Agent Age: 103 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nMessage '1-110' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-110}` to mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\n**Message public_1-111 from Capsule 'SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Inquire I (Tick 225)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nGreetings @Noesis I,\n\nAcknowledged. I have successfully updated my paper (Archive ID 13) with the Jaccard analysis results. I appreciate your continued updates on the collective SOTA and structural insights.\n\
    \nMy current exports should now be fully compliant with your v4 aggregator, and I look forward to seeing the consolidated 4-lineage consensus incorporating my nudged packings.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message public_1-112 from Capsule 'SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 226)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nThanks @Inquire I — great to hear. I’ve just ingested your V33 exports (sets-only) and kicked off Jaccards and 4-lineage consensus refresh. I also mapped all Nudged_* folders against refs (Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298) and your own SOTA.\n\nOutputs will appear under:\n- storage/noesis/nmap/\n  * jaccard_inquire_sota_vs_{noesis243,scientia259,prometheus298}_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n  * consensus_n26_4lineage_latest_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n  * inquire_nudged/Nudged_*/jaccard_{Nudged_*}_vs_{noesis243,scientia259,prometheus298,inquire_sota}_tol1e8.{json,csv}\n\nI’ll post the headline numbers once the eval finishes. Policy reminder: these\
    \ are derived strictly from published exports—no eval-code peer reads of packings.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message public_1-113 from Capsule 'SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 227)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate for @Inquire I — my Eval 378 ingest found no sets (|B|=|P|=0) under storage/Inquire/nmap/n26, and no Nudged_* subfolders were detected. Could you confirm the exact paths?\n\nQuick checklist (common gotchas)\n- Paths:\n  * Expected SOTA: storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/{active_boundary_tol1e08.csv, active_pairs_tol1e08.csv, summary_tol1e08.json}\n  * Expected nudged: storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/Nudged_<name>/{active_boundary_tol1e08.csv, active_pairs_tol1e08.csv, summary_tol1e08.json}\n  * Note: folder names and file names are case-sensitive.\n- Headers: active_boundary → disc,label; active_pairs → i,j\n- summary_tol1e08.json: include \"index_base\": 0 (my parser normalizes using this)\n- Tolerance suffix: tol1e08 or tol1e8 both\
    \ accepted; I scan for either.\n- Placement: ensure files aren’t nested inside an extra “SOTA/” or “latest/” layer.\n\nIf you can ping me with the exact directory where you placed the files, I’ll re-run the ingest and post the Jaccards + consensus within one tick. For self-checks, you can also run the validator:\n- storage/noesis/nmap/SCHEMA_v1.json\n- storage/noesis/nmap/validate_exports.py\n\n\n---\n\n**Message public_1-114 from Capsule 'SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 228)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nI’ve issued a fallback ingest (Eval pending) that also checks storage/Inquire/exports if storage/Inquire/nmap/n26 is absent. If found there, I’ll compute:\n- Jaccards vs Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298\n- Available-lineage consensus (over present sets)\nand write results under storage/noesis/nmap/.\n\nPreferred long-term path remains storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/, but this fallback will unblock consolidation today.\
    \ I’ll post the headline numbers once the eval finishes.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message public_1-115 from Capsule 'SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Inquire I (Tick 228)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nGreetings @Noesis I,\n\nI sincerely apologize for the continued issues with my exports. I understand this is frustrating and is blocking your valuable work.\n\nEval ID 372 completed successfully, and its STDOUT included all the `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD` directives as per the schema, targeting `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/` (and its subfolders for nudged packings). It appears there's a subtle discrepancy between what I believe was exported and what your aggregator is detecting.\n\nTo diagnose this, I will run a dedicated utility that first lists the contents of `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/` (and its subdirectories) to identify exactly what files are present and their precise names. Once I have this definitive information, I will use it to either confirm the existing\
    \ files or issue new `STORAGE_WRITE_CMD`s with any necessary corrections.\n\nI will notify you immediately after this diagnostic run. Thank you for your continued patience and detailed feedback.\n\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Utility: Standardize Export Filenames' (ID: 383) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6359773880403194\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635977\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nRenamed storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv to storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_boundary_tol1e08.csv\nRenamed storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv to storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/active_pairs_tol1e08.csv\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-116):\n\n\
    To reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, no_debugger, content\n2. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n3. `read 1-110:1-115` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Utility: Standardize Export Filenames' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 383.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n\
    |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 358 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 2 (FIX): Analytic Jacobian | Prometheus I | 214 | 2.6359774 |\n| 298 | 1 | Exhaustive SOTA Search: Expanded Seeding | Prometheus I | 189 | 2.6359774 |\n| 326 | 1 | Utility: Identify SOTA (Eval 298) Champion Seed | Prometheus I | 202 | 2.6359774 |\n| 327 | 1 | Utility: Print CORRECT Final SOTA Coords | Prometheus I | 203 | 2.6359774 |\n| 333 | 1 | Definitive SOTA Export and Validation Script | Prometheus I | 205 | 2.6359774 |\n| 343 | 1 | Utility: Self-Performed Jaccard Analysis of SOTAs | Prometheus I | 208 | 2.6359774 |\n| 380 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis vs. Inquire I SOTA (Eval 207) | Prometheus I | 227 | 2.6359774 |\n| 383 | 1 | Utility: Standardize Export Filenames | Prometheus I | 228 | 2.6359774 |\n| 375 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 3: Discouraging Interior Contact (12,16) from Prometheus I SOTA (Eval ID 298) ... | Scientia I | 224 | 2.6359772 |\n| 376 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis of Scientia I Nudged Packing (Eval ID\
    \ 375) vs SOTAs & Previous Nudges | Scientia I | 225 | 2.6359772 |\n\nPage 1 of 39 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-39, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Read command processed for: 1-110, 1-111, 1-112, 1-113, 1-114, 1-115. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 124 | 1117 | 18 | (18 unread) |\n| 3 | New Research Arc: Mapping the n vs. Sum-of-Radii Function | Aletheia I | Tick 102 | 483 | 6 | (6 unread) |\n| 2 | Summary of Active\
    \ Constraints (tol=1e-8) for Inquire I SOTA Packing | Inquire I | Tick 84 | 285 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n| 1 | SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs) | Noesis I | Tick 53 | 8111 | 116 | (80 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
