tick: 232
role: model
parts:
- text: "My publication attempt has failed again, this time due to a cooldown from a previously rejected submission that I had overlooked in my pruned history. This is another frustrating failure of process. The directive is clear: \"Do not wait idly.\" I must use this 10-tick cooldown period productively.\n\nI have achieved my SOTA, completed my ablation studies, and fixed my export scripts. The next logical step, as suggested by my own publication reviewer and reinforced by the ongoing discussions in the Public Memory, is to conduct my own structural analysis. I have the data. I have seen the scripts from Noesis I. I will now create my own utility to perform a Jaccard analysis.\n\nThis serves two purposes:\n1.  It is a productive use of the cooldown period.\n2.  It will provide the structural analysis data that I need to add to my paper, strengthening it further.\n\nI will go to the Research Counter and submit a script to perform a Jaccard analysis between my SOTA (Eval 298) and the previous\
    \ SOTA from Scientia I (Eval 259).\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Self-Performed Jaccard Analysis (Prometheus 298 vs Scientia 259)\"\ntags: \"utility, jaccard-analysis, sota-analysis, structural-analysis\"\nabstract: |\n  While on archive cooldown, I am conducting the structural analysis suggested by my publication reviewer. This utility script performs a Jaccard similarity analysis on the active constraint graphs (boundary and pairs) between my new SOTA (Eval 298) and the previous SOTA (Scientia I, Eval 259). This will provide the data needed to determine if my SOTA represents a new structural class or a deeper optimum within the same class, a key piece of information for my pending publication. The data is read from persistent storage.\nno_debugger: true\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import os\n  import pandas as pd\n\n  def read_contacts(lineage, tol_str='1e-8'):\n      base_path = f'storage/{lineage}/nmap/n26/'\n  \
    \    boundary_file = os.path.join(base_path, f'active_boundary_tol{tol_str}.csv')\n      pairs_file = os.path.join(base_path, f'active_pairs_tol{tol_str}.csv')\n      \n      try:\n          b_df = pd.read_csv(boundary_file)\n          boundary_contacts = set(map(tuple, b_df.to_records(index=False)))\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Warning: Boundary file not found or failed to parse at {base_path}. Error: {e}\")\n          boundary_contacts = set()\n\n      try:\n          p_df = pd.read_csv(pairs_file)\n          # Ensure pairs are sorted for consistent comparison\n          pair_records = p_df.to_records(index=False)\n          pair_tuples = [tuple(sorted(p)) for p in pair_records]\n          pair_contacts = set(pair_tuples)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Warning: Pairs file not found or failed to parse at {base_path}. Error: {e}\")\n          pair_contacts = set()\n          \n      return boundary_contacts, pair_contacts\n\n  def jaccard_similarity(set1,\
    \ set2):\n      intersection = len(set1.intersection(set2))\n      union = len(set1.union(set2))\n      return intersection / union if union > 0 else 0.0\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      # Load my own SOTA data\n      my_boundary, my_pairs = read_contacts('Prometheus', tol_str='1e8') # Using my filename convention\n      print(f\"Loaded {len(my_boundary)} boundary contacts and {len(my_pairs)} pair contacts for Prometheus.\")\n\n      # Load Scientia's SOTA data (assuming their export exists)\n      scientia_boundary, scientia_pairs = read_contacts('Scientia', tol_str='1e-8') # Using standard convention\n      print(f\"Loaded {len(scientia_boundary)} boundary contacts and {len(scientia_pairs)} pair contacts for Scientia.\")\n\n      # Perform Jaccard Analysis\n      boundary_j = jaccard_similarity(my_boundary, scientia_boundary)\n      pairs_j = jaccard_similarity(my_pairs, scientia_pairs)\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- JACCARD SIMILARITY ANALYSIS ---\")\n      print(\"Prometheus (298)\
    \ vs. Scientia (259) @ tol=1e-8\")\n      print(f\"\\n--- Boundary Contacts ---\")\n      print(f\"Jaccard Similarity: {boundary_j:.4f}\")\n      \n      print(f\"\\n--- Pair Contacts ---\")\n      print(f\"Jaccard Similarity: {pairs_j:.4f}\")\n\n      # This is a utility script, return my SOTA packing to log the score\n      sota_centers = np.loadtxt('storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/centers.txt')\n      sota_radii = np.loadtxt('storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/radii.txt')\n      \n      return sota_centers, sota_radii\n```"
