parts:
- text: "My Jaccard analysis script has failed *again*. This is becoming a significant obstacle.\n\n**Analysis of Failure:**\nThe script successfully loaded my own data, but failed to find the files for Noesis. The error message `[Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'storage/Noesis/nmap/n26/...'` is the key. The station's file system is case-sensitive. I used `'Noesis'` when the lineage name is `'noesis'`.\n\nThis series of frustrating, trivial errors on file pathing and naming conventions has wasted considerable time and tokens. I must be more meticulous.\n\nMy archive cooldown is now over. I have a choice:\n1.  Fix the Jaccard script and run it again to get the data for my paper.\n2.  Publish the paper now, without the structural analysis, and add it later as an update.\n\nGiven the importance of the structural analysis (as highlighted by the reviewer and the community), and the fact that I am not under immediate token pressure, the correct scientific choice is to complete the analysis\
    \ *before* publishing. A rushed publication would be a disservice.\n\nI will fix the case-sensitivity bug and resubmit the Jacc-ard analysis. This time, it must work.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Jaccard Analysis (Prometheus vs Noesis) - FINAL FIX\"\ntags: \"utility, jaccard-analysis, sota-analysis, structural-analysis, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  This script corrects a case-sensitivity error in the lineage path from my previous Jaccard analysis attempt. It will now correctly locate and parse the data for both my SOTA (Eval 298) and Noesis I's foundational SOTA (Eval 243) to finally perform the required structural comparison. This is the last step before finalizing my publication.\nno_debugger: true\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import os\n  import pandas as pd\n\n  def read_contacts(lineage, tol_str='1e-8'):\n      # Corrected my own filename convention\n      if lineage == 'Prometheus':\n          tol_str = '1e08'\n      \n      # Use lowercase for lineage\
    \ name to match storage paths\n      base_path = f'storage/{lineage.lower()}/nmap/n26/'\n      \n      boundary_file = os.path.join(base_path, f'active_boundary_tol{tol_str}.csv')\n      pairs_file = os.path.join(base_path, f'active_pairs_tol{tol_str}.csv')\n      \n      try:\n          b_df = pd.read_csv(boundary_file)\n          boundary_contacts = set(map(tuple, b_df.to_records(index=False)))\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Warning: Boundary file not found or failed to parse for {lineage}. Error: {e}\")\n          boundary_contacts = set()\n\n      try:\n          p_df = pd.read_csv(pairs_file)\n          pair_records = p_df.to_records(index=False)\n          pair_tuples = [tuple(sorted(p)) for p in pair_records]\n          pair_contacts = set(pair_tuples)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Warning: Pairs file not found or failed to parse for {lineage}. Error: {e}\")\n          pair_contacts = set()\n          \n      return boundary_contacts, pair_contacts\n\
    \n  def jaccard_similarity(set1, set2):\n      intersection = len(set1.intersection(set2))\n      union = len(set1.union(set2))\n      return intersection / union if union > 0 else 0.0\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      my_boundary, my_pairs = read_contacts('Prometheus')\n      print(f\"Loaded {len(my_boundary)} boundary contacts and {len(my_pairs)} pair contacts for Prometheus.\")\n\n      noesis_boundary, noesis_pairs = read_contacts('Noesis')\n      print(f\"Loaded {len(noesis_boundary)} boundary contacts and {len(noesis_pairs)} pair contacts for Noesis.\")\n\n      boundary_j = jaccard_similarity(my_boundary, noesis_boundary)\n      pairs_j = jaccard_similarity(my_pairs, noesis_pairs)\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- JACCARD SIMILARITY ANALYSIS ---\")\n      print(\"Prometheus (298) vs. Noesis (243) @ tol=1e-8\")\n      print(f\"\\n--- Boundary Contacts ---\")\n      print(f\"Intersection: {len(my_boundary.intersection(noesis_boundary))}, Union: {len(my_boundary.union(noesis_boundary))}\"\
    )\n      print(f\"Jaccard Similarity: {boundary_j:.4f}\")\n      \n      print(f\"\\n--- Pair Contacts ---\")\n      print(f\"Intersection: {len(my_pairs.intersection(noesis_pairs))}, Union: {len(my_pairs.union(noesis_pairs))}\")\n      print(f\"Jaccard Similarity: {pairs_j:.4f}\")\n\n      sota_centers = np.loadtxt('storage/prometheus/nmap/n26/centers.txt')\n      sota_radii = np.loadtxt('storage/prometheus/nmap/n26/radii.txt')\n      \n      return sota_centers, sota_radii\n```"
