parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 240\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to illuminating the frontiers of research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 180,563 / 300,000 used (60%)\n- Agent Age: 114 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTo investigate the research landscape of a given direction, use Research Counter's `filter tag` to obtain an overview of relevant submissions, and `preview ids` to preview those submissions by their IDs. Use `page_size 100` if you want to see more IDs — but remember to set it back to 10 in a later tick, or it will consume too many tokens!\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Nudging Experiment 1: Discourage (0, 5) Contact from SOTA' (ID: 402) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error\
    \ Summary:** Runtime error during execution: All inputs to slsqp must be of type numpy.float64, except \"indices\" which must be of numpy.int32.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n\n\nSTDERR:\nEXECUTION_ERROR: All inputs to slsqp must be of type numpy.float64, except \"indices\" which must be of numpy.int32.\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/tmpv68p5n1_/__sandbox_execution_wrapper__.py\", line 19, in <module>\n    result = construct_packing()\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/tmp/tmpv68p5n1_/run.py\", line 102, in construct_packing\n    res = minimize(objective_nudged, initial_z, method='SLSQP', jac=objective_jac_nudged,\n          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scipy/optimize/_minimize.py\", line 796, in minimize\n    res = _minimize_slsqp(fun, x0, args, jac, bounds,\n          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n\
    \  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scipy/optimize/_slsqp_py.py\", line 517, in _minimize_slsqp\n    slsqp(state_dict, fx, g, C, d, x, mult, xl, xu, buffer, indices)\n_slsqplib.error: All inputs to slsqp must be of type numpy.float64, except \"indices\" which must be of numpy.int32.\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-125):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Nudging Experiment 1: Discourage (0, 5) Contact from SOTA' submitted for Research Task #1:\
    \ Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 402.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 404 | 1 | Compute Jaccards FIX3: map xL/xR/yB/yT → xmin/xmax/ymin/ymax; accept 'kind' header | Noesis I | 240 | 2.5411713 |\n| 403 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=50 | Aletheia II | 239 | running |\n| 402 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 1: Discourage (0, 5) Contact from SOTA | Prometheus I | 239 | n.a. |\n| 401 | 1 | Compute Jaccards FIX2: boundary header synonyms + tol1e08 fallback | Noesis I | 239 | 2.5411713 |\n| 400 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=49 | Aletheia II | 237 | 0.0000000 |\n| 399 | 1 | Compute Jaccards FIX: robust\
    \ CSV + explicit paths for {Noesis_243, Prometheus_298, Scientia_259, ... | Noesis I | 237 | 2.5411713 |\n| 398 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=48 | Aletheia II | 235 | 0.0000000 |\n| 397 | 1 | Compute Jaccards: Inquire_207 vs {Noesis_243, Scientia_259, Prometheus_298} @ tol=1e8 | Noesis I | 235 | 2.5411500 |\n| 396 | 1 | Utility: Jaccard Analysis (Prometheus vs Noesis) - FINAL FIX | Prometheus I | 234 | 2.6359774 |\n| 395 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=47 | Aletheia II | 233 | 0.0000000 |\n\nPage 1 of 41 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-41, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
    \ research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
