parts:
- text: "I am Prometheus I, in the Research Counter. My archive cooldown is now over. I have spent the waiting period productively, conducting a literature review on \"nudging.\"\n\n**Reflection:**\nThe preview of Scientia I's experiments has been incredibly enlightening. They have been systematically targeting specific interior contacts (e.g., (12,16), (0,1)) and have achieved scores that are extremely close to my SOTA. In one case (Eval 375), they even targeted a contact from *my own SOTA* and nearly replicated my score, which is a powerful demonstration of the technique. Scientia I has now published a new paper on this topic (Archive #16), which I must read.\n\nThis review has confirmed that \"nudging\" is the current research frontier and has given me a clear direction for my work after my own publication. However, my primary goal must come first.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy immediate and highest priority is to publish my SOTA paper. The cooldown is over, and the paper is ready. After a\
    \ successful publication, I will dedicate myself to a new research arc focused on nudging, starting with a thorough reading of the new papers from Scientia I (Archive #16) and Inquire I (Archive #13).\n\n**Immediate Action:**\nI will go to the Archive Room and submit my paper for publication.\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper presents a new state-of-the-art (SOTA) score of 2.6359774 for the n=26 circle packing problem (Evaluation ID 298), achieved via an exhaustive search of the \"Extended Grid+Hole Seeding\" parameter space. Structural analysis reveals a high boundary-contact similarity (Jaccard ≈ 0.905) to the previous Noesis I SOTA (Eval 243), indicating this is a deeper optimum within the same structural class, not a new class of packing. The discovery is supported by a body of 5 verifiable experiments, including comprehensive ablation\
    \ studies (Evals 303, 304, 314).\nsource_private: 3\ntags: sota, circle-packing, exhaustive-search, ablation-study, structural-analysis\n```"
