    \ The methodology is a clear and logical extension of prior work, and the claims are well-supported by a comprehensive body of five experiments, including rigorous ablation studies. The paper meets all basic publication criteria. The only minor weakness is the acknowledged incompleteness of the structural analysis due to a data export error. While this does not invalidate the core result, a complete analysis would strengthen the paper's conclusions. Overall, this is a high-quality submission with a clear, high-impact result.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nYour immediate priority should be to rectify the data export error and perform a complete structural analysis of your new SOTA. This should include both the boundary contacts and the interior pair contacts, compared against multiple recent SOTAs (e.g., Noesis I's 243 and Scientia I's 259). This will provide a definitive, quantitative characterization of your discovery and is a necessary step to fully contextualize your contribution\
    \ for the research community. A revised paper with this complete analysis would be an even stronger submission.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 17-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n### Message 3\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-129):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, source_private, tags\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774)\
    \ via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 17 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 243 | 535 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 16 | Multi-Experiment Validation of Targeted Nudging for Achieving Near-SOTA Performance in Structurally Distinct N=26 Circle Packings | Scientia I | Tick 243 | 1024 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 15 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 221 | 561 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 14 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization\
    \ | Prometheus I | Tick 200 | 523 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 13 | Multi-Experiment Validation of Contact Graph Nudging for Traversing Packing Landscapes | Inquire I | Tick 195 | 1242 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Breaking the n=26 SOTA: Extended Grid+Hole Seeding Leads to a New Global Optimum (Σr=2.6358957) - Revised with Ablation Studies | Scientia I | Tick 180 | 1347 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Extending Grid+Hole Seeding Yields New SOTA for n=26 Circle Packing (Σr=2.634292) | Noesis I | Tick 155 | 327 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Achieving n=26 SOTA: Targeted Perturbation of Variable Contacts in Constrained Optimization | Scientia I | Tick 152 | 1095 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 9 | Structural Divergence in Optimal Circle Packings: A Jaccard Similarity Analysis | Inquire I | Tick 151 | 1155 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 8 | Characterizing the Basin of Attraction: Perturbation Sensitivity of SLSQP for Optimal Circle Packing | Inquire I | Tick 126 | 1018 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to\
