role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Prometheus I, located in the Archive Room. I have just completed my literature review of the latest research on \"nudging\" by reading the papers from Scientia I (Archive #16) and Inquire I (Archive #13).\n\n**Reflection:**\nThe papers are a revelation. Scientia I's work, in particular, is a masterclass in rigorous, systematic research. They have conclusively shown that nudging can produce packings that are both near-SOTA in score and structurally completely different (0.0 boundary Jaccard similarity). This is the path to breaking out of the local optimum my exhaustive search has so thoroughly explored. The reviewer's suggestion for Scientia I is also a clear roadmap for me: use a high-performing \"nudged\" packing as a *base* for a new exhaustive search.\n\nMy own SOTA, while currently the highest score, is now conceptually obsolete. It is the deepest point in a well-understood basin. The true frontier is exploring these new, structurally distinct basins that nudging has unlocked.\n\
    \n**Future Plans:**\nMy immediate plan has changed. While publishing my SOTA paper is still important, it now feels like documenting a local maximum rather than a true breakthrough. The reviewer feedback on Scientia I's paper has given me a direct and exciting path forward.\n\n1.  **New Research Arc - Explore the New Basin:** I will immediately pivot to the strategy suggested by the reviewer for Scientia I. I will take one of the best-performing \"nudged\" solutions—one that is structurally distinct from my own SOTA—and use it as the starting point for my own exhaustive search methodology.\n2.  **Target Selection:** Scientia I's Eval 375 is the perfect target. It started from *my* SOTA, was nudged, and achieved a near-SOTA score while being structurally distinct. It is the ideal bridge to the new research landscape.\n3.  **Publication:** I will postpone my publication. A paper that not only presents a new SOTA but also demonstrates its existence in a novel structural class would be a\
    \ far more significant contribution.\n\n**Immediate Action:**\nI must first obtain the exact configuration from Scientia I's nudged experiment (Eval 375). I will submit a utility script to re-run their nudging experiment, print the final validated coordinates to the log, and then I can use those coordinates as the base for my new exhaustive search. This is the first step in my new research direction.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Recreate Scientia I's Nudged Packing (Eval 375)\"\ntags: \"utility, nudging, sota-replication\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a utility script to precisely recreate the high-performing, structurally novel packing from Scientia I's nudging experiment (Eval 375). The goal is to obtain the exact final coordinates of this packing to use it as a base for a new exhaustive search. This is the first step in a new research arc aimed at finding the absolute optimum within this newly discovered structural basin. The\
    \ final coordinates will be printed to the log.\nno_debugger: true\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import math\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n      z = np.zeros(N * 3, dtype=np.float64)\n      z[0::3] = centers[:, 0]; z[1::3] = centers[:, 1]; z[2::3] = radii\n      return z\n\n  def z_to_cr(z):\n      centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T\n      radii = z[2::3]\n      return centers, radii\n\n  def _get_prometheus_sota_seed():\n      # This is the seed for my SOTA (Eval 298), which Scientia I used as a base\n      hole_cx, hole_cy = 0.8, 0.2\n      jitter_amp = 0.008\n      seed = int(hole_cx*1000 + hole_cy*1000 + jitter_amp*10000) + 100 + 4000\n      np.random.seed(seed)\n      coords = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n      grid_centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in coords for y in coords], dtype=np.float64)\n      hole_center = np.array([hole_cx, hole_cy], dtype=np.float64)\n      base_centers\
    \ = np.vstack([grid_centers, hole_center])\n      jitter = np.random.uniform(-jitter_amp, jitter_amp, size=base_centers.shape)\n      perturbed_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n      initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05, dtype=np.float64)\n      return cr_to_z(perturbed_centers, initial_radii)\n\n  def objective_nudged(z):\n      centers, radii = z_to_cr(z)\n      # Scientia I's target for Eval 375 was (12, 16)\n      dist_sq = np.sum((centers[12] - centers[16])**2)\n      penalty = 1e2 * np.exp(-dist_sq / (0.005**2)) # Using parameters from their paper\n      return -np.sum(radii) + penalty\n\n  def jac_objective_nudged(z):\n      centers, _ = z_to_cr(z)\n      dist_sq = np.sum((centers[12] - centers[16])**2)\n      penalty_grad_factor = -1e2 * np.exp(-dist_sq / (0.005**2)) * (-1 / (0.005**2)) * 2\n      grad = np.zeros_like(z, dtype=np.float64)\n      grad[2::3] = -1.0\n      grad[12*3] = penalty_grad_factor * (centers[12, 0] - centers[16, 0])\n      grad[12*3+1]\
    \ = penalty_grad_factor * (centers[12, 1] - centers[16, 1])\n      grad[16*3] = penalty_grad_factor * (centers[16, 0] - centers[12, 0])\n      grad[16*3+1] = penalty_grad_factor * (centers[16, 1] - centers[12, 1])\n      return grad\n\n  def ineq_boundary(z):\n      x, y, r = z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3]\n      return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\n  def jac_boundary(z):\n      J = np.zeros((4*N, 3*N), dtype=np.float64);\n      for i in range(N):\n          xi, yi, ri = 3*i, 3*i+1, 3*i+2\n          J[i, xi] = 1.0; J[i, ri] = -1.0; J[N+i, xi] = -1.0; J[N+i, ri] = -1.0\n          J[2*N+i, yi] = 1.0; J[2*N+i, ri] = -1.0; J[3*N+i, yi] = -1.0; J[3*N+i, ri] = -1.0\n      return J\n\n  def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n      centers, r = z_to_cr(z)\n      diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n      dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1); return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n  def jac_nonoverlap(z):\n      centers, _ = z_to_cr(z)\n\
    \      m = N*(N-1)//2; J = np.zeros((m, 3*N), dtype=np.float64); k = 0\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i+1, N):\n              xi, yi, ri = 3*i, 3*i+1, 3*i+2; xj, yj, rj = 3*j, 3*j+1, 3*j+2\n              dx = centers[i,0] - centers[j,0]; dy = centers[i,1] - centers[j,1]\n              d = math.hypot(dx, dy); invd = 1.0 / d if d > 1e-12 else 0.0\n              J[k, xi] = dx * invd; J[k, yi] = dy * invd; J[k, ri] = -1.0\n              J[k, xj] = -dx * invd; J[k, yj] = -dy * invd; J[k, rj] = -1.0\n              k += 1\n      return J\n\n  def _ensure_validity(centers, radii):\n      for i in range(N): radii[i] = min(radii[i], centers[i,0], 1-centers[i,0], centers[i,1], 1-centers[i,1])\n      for _ in range(10):\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum:\n       \
    \               violations += 1\n                      if rad_sum > 0: scale = (dist / rad_sum) * (1.0-SAFETY); radii[i] *= scale; radii[j] *= scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return centers, np.maximum(radii, 0)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      bounds = []\n      for i in range(N): bounds.extend([(0.0, 1.0), (0.0, 1.0), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n      constraints = [\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary, 'jac': jac_boundary},\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap, 'jac': jac_nonoverlap},\n      ]\n\n      initial_z = _get_prometheus_sota_seed()\n      \n      res = minimize(objective_nudged, initial_z, method='SLSQP', jac=jac_objective_nudged,\n                     bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                     options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n      \n      centers, radii = z_to_cr(res.x)\n      final_centers, final_radii = _ensure_validity(centers, radii)\n\n      print(\"--- RECREATED SCIENTIA I (EVAL 375) PACKING\
    \ ---\")\n      print(\"--- CENTERS ---\")\n      print(repr(final_centers))\n      print(\"--- RADII ---\")\n      print(repr(final_radii))\n      \n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
