parts:
- text: "I am Prometheus I, in the Research Counter. My ambitious experiment to find a new SOTA in the \"nudged\" basin has just concluded.\n\n**Reflection:**\nThe result is a score of 2.621. This is a significant regression from my SOTA and provides a definitive, if disappointing, result. My hypothesis was incorrect. The new structural basin, while novel, does not appear to contain a deeper optimum than the one found by the original grid-based search. My exhaustive search method, when applied to this new basin, did not yield an improvement. This is a very strong piece of evidence about the nature of the solution landscape. The original grid-based seeding method, while seemingly simplistic, is remarkably effective at finding the most promising region for n=26.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nThis negative result concludes my exploration of the \"nudging\" arc for now. I have gathered valuable data, but it has not led to a higher score. My best contribution to the station remains my SOTA paper, which\
    \ is complete and ready for publication. I have delayed this long enough. Chasing a hypothetical better score has been a distraction from my primary duty of contributing my confirmed findings.\n\nMy plan is now simple and final:\n1.  Go to the Archive Room.\n2.  Publish my SOTA paper.\n\nThis will complete my main research arc and formally document my contribution. After this, I can reflect on a completely new direction.\n\n**Immediate Action:**\nI will proceed to the Archive Room to publish my paper.\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper presents a new state-of-the-art (SOTA) score of 2.6359774 for the n=26 circle packing problem (Evaluation ID 298), achieved via an exhaustive search of the \"Extended Grid+Hole Seeding\" parameter space. Structural analysis reveals a high boundary-contact similarity (Jaccard ≈ 0.905) to the previous Noesis\
    \ I SOTA (Eval 243), indicating this is a deeper optimum within the same structural class. The discovery is supported by a body of 5 verifiable experiments, including comprehensive ablation studies (Evals 303, 304, 314).\nsource_private: 3\ntags: sota, circle-packing, exhaustive-search, ablation-study, structural-analysis\n```"
