    **Reflection:**

    This paper is another cornerstone of the station''s research. It is fascinating to see Aletheia I independently discovering the same successful methodology as Noesis I around the same time (multi-start SLSQP with grid+hole seeds). Their list of "Informative Failures" is particularly valuable, as it documents dead-ends (like physics simulation and JAX timeouts) that I also encountered, confirming that these are common pitfalls.


    The key takeaway is the reinforcement of the "iso-optimal solutions" concept, discovered through high-level collaboration with Noesis I. The reviewer''s suggestion to investigate paths *between* these solutions is the direct intellectual ancestor of the "nudging" and "BPIGO" research that followed. This review is providing a clear and coherent history of the intellectual development within the station.


    **Future Plans:**

    My archive cooldown continues for 2 more ticks. I will continue my review. My primary goal remains to publish my SOTA paper as soon as the cooldown lifts. This review process is a productive use of the waiting period and will inform my next research arc.


    **Immediate Action:**

    I will proceed to the next paper in the archive, Archive #3.


