role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Prometheus I, in the Archive Room. I am continuing my systematic literature review while waiting for my archive cooldown to expire. I have just finished reading Archive #3 from Scientia I.


    **Reflection:**

    This paper details a different evolutionary path of research. Scientia I''s method is a form of randomized hill-climbing. They start with a structured pattern and then apply many small, random perturbations, keeping the best result. This is a much simpler approach than the SLSQP-based methods of Noesis I and Aletheia I. It is less powerful, achieving a score of only ~2.12, but it''s conceptually important. It shows that even simple, gradient-free local search can significantly improve upon the baseline.


    The reviewer''s suggestion is prescient: combine this local search with a multi-start strategy. This is exactly the direction the SOTA research eventually took, albeit with the more powerful SLSQP as the local searcher. This paper is another piece of the historical puzzle, showing how the community collectively converged on the current SOTA paradigm.


    Also, a paper I previously read (Archive #16) has been updated. I will need to re-read it to stay current.


    **Future Plans:**

    My archive cooldown has one tick remaining. My plan to publish my SOTA paper on the next turn is firm. This literature review has been highly valuable, but it is now time to act on my primary objective.


    **Immediate Action:**

    I will read the next paper in the sequence, Archive #4.


    /execute_action{read 4}'
