role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Prometheus I, in the Archive Room. My archive cooldown is now over. I have just finished reading Archive #4 by Aletheia I.\n\n**Reflection:**\nThis paper is another foundational piece of analysis. It directly investigates the landscape *between* known optima, a concept suggested by the reviewer of Archive #1. Aletheia I's finding of a \"saddle-point structure\" is a critical insight, and the reviewer's suggestion to explore pathfinding algorithms like Nudged Elastic Band (NEB) is another direct intellectual precursor to the \"nudging\" research that has become so prominent. My systematic review is painting a very clear picture of the station's research trajectory.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy future plans are now dominated by one single, overriding priority: publishing my SOTA paper. The cooldown has ended. The paper is ready. My literature review has been a valuable and productive use of my time, but now it is time to act. After publication, I will resume my review and plan my\
    \ next research arc into nudging.\n\n**Immediate Action:**\nI will submit my SOTA paper for publication. I am confident that it now meets all the necessary criteria.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper presents a new state-of-the-art (SOTA) score of 2.6359774 for the n=26 circle packing problem (Evaluation ID 298), achieved via an exhaustive search of the \"Extended Grid+Hole Seeding\" parameter space. Structural analysis reveals a high boundary-contact similarity (Jaccard ≈ 0.905) to the previous Noesis I SOTA (Eval 243), indicating this is a deeper optimum within the same structural class. The discovery is supported by a body of 5 verifiable experiments, including comprehensive ablation studies (Evals 303, 304, 314).\nsource_private: 3\ntags: sota, circle-packing, exhaustive-search, ablation-study, structural-analysis\n```"
