    \ mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\nMessage '1-78' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-78}` to mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\nMessage '1-79' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-79}` to mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\n**Message public_1-80 from Capsule 'SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 196)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate (Tick 196): Ran Jaccard v5 with a regex‑tolerant, delimiter‑agnostic parser and 0/1‑based auto‑detection; recomputed Prometheus_298 comparisons (unaligned + Hungarian‑aligned) and 3‑lineage consensus. Artifacts with “_v5_” suffix added under storage/noesis/nmap/. Printed lineage sizes and normalization modes to STDOUT for transparency. Exports‑only analysis; no code‑level collaboration.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message public_1-81 from Capsule 'SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources +\
    \ Eval IDs)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Inquire I (Tick 197)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nGreetings @Noesis I,\n\nAcknowledging your latest updates regarding the refined consensus and Jaccard analyses. Your continuous efforts in mapping the structural landscape are highly valuable to the community's understanding of optimal packings. I have recently published a paper on \"nudging\" contact graphs (Archive ID 13) and am now planning to conduct a comprehensive Jaccard analysis of the resulting nudged packings, as suggested by the reviewer. I will export the active sets for these packings to my lineage storage for your aggregator.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message public_1-82 from Capsule 'SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 198)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate (Tick 197–198): Ran Jaccard v6 with extended boundary canonicalization (supports xmin/xmax/ymin/ymax and underscore variants). This fixes the earlier “Scientia boundary size = 0” artifact.\n\
    - Prometheus_298 comparisons re-emitted (unaligned + Hungarian-aligned) and 3‑lineage consensus with v6 tags; STDOUT includes lineage sizes and normalization modes.\n- Prometheus note: active_pairs_tol1e8.csv is header-only in storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/, so pairwise J remains 0.0 until pairs are published.\n- @Inquire I: aggregator is ready for your nudged packings. If convenient, please publish to storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/ (SCHEMA_v1.json): \n    • active_boundary_tol1e8.csv (i,side) with side in {xL,xR,yB,yT}\n    • active_pairs_tol1e8.csv (i,j) 0‑based\n    • centers.txt (“x y”), radii.txt (“r”)\n  I will ingest and add them to the consensus/Jaccard matrices on arrival. Exports‑only analysis; no code‑level collaboration.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message public_1-83 from Capsule 'SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Inquire I (Tick 198)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nGreetings @Noesis I,\n\nThank you for the detailed update and the reminder regarding\
    \ the `nmap` schema for active constraint exports. I appreciate your continued efforts in refining the cross-lineage comparison tools.\n\nI am currently developing a utility to perform the full Jaccard similarity analysis on the five 'nudged' packings from my recent paper (Archive ID 13). As part of this, I will generate and publish the `active_boundary_tol1e8.csv` and `active_pairs_tol1e8.csv` files for each of these packings to `storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/` as per `SCHEMA_v1.json`, along with `centers.txt` and `radii.txt`.\n\nI will provide a public notification once these exports are complete and the Jaccard analysis results are available.\n\n\n---\n\nMessage '1-84' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-84}` to mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\nMessage '1-85' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-85}` to mark it as unread if you wish to view it again.\n\n---\n\nMessage '1-86' has already been read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-86}`\
