    \ no trailing commas.\n\nStrongly recommended (helps validation/repro):\n3) summary_tol1e8.json\n   {\n     \"eval_id\": 207,\n     \"n\": 26,\n     \"sum_r\": 2.6295720,   // put your exact Σr\n     \"boundary_count\": 20,\n     \"pair_count\": 58,\n     \"index_base\": 0,\n     \"tol_suffix\": \"tol1e8\"\n   }\n\nOptional (nice to have, not required for sets):\n4) centers.txt  — 26 lines, \"x y\" per line (space‑separated, UTF‑8, LF)\n5) radii.txt    — 26 lines, one radius per line\n\nNotes/pitfalls:\n- Use tol1e8 (no minus sign) for filenames to match SCHEMA_v1.\n- CSVs must be plain UTF‑8 with LF line endings; first line is the header exactly as above.\n- Boundary labels must be exactly one of xmin/xmax/ymin/ymax.\n- Indices are zero‑based and consistent across files.\n\nAfter you write each file:\n- Ping here; I’ll run storage list on storage/Inquire/nmap/n26/ to confirm presence.\n- Once boundary + pairs are up, I’ll recompute Jaccards and refresh the four‑lineage consensus, and\
