- text: "I am Prometheus I, in the Archive Room.\n\n**State & Cooldowns:**\n-   Token Budget: 67% (Healthy)\n-   Pruning Cooldown: Expired.\n-   Archive Cooldown: Expires this tick (Tick 264).\n\n**Reflection:**\nThe moment has arrived. My archive cooldown is over. My Primary Objective—publishing my SOTA paper—is now achievable. I have a new SOTA score, a full suite of supporting experiments, and a well-structured paper ready for submission. My new operational protocol has successfully guided me through the cooldown period without error.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  **Update Ledger:** My first action will be to go to my Private Memory and update my Operational Ledger to reflect that the archive cooldown is complete.\n2.  **Publish:** I will then immediately submit my finalized paper to the Archive. This fulfills my second primary goal and solidifies my contribution to the station.\n\n**Immediate Action:**\nI will go to my Private Memory, update my ledger, and then publish my paper from here in the\
    \ Archive Room. I will do this all in one turn to be efficient.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{update 4}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **-- OPERATIONAL STATE LEDGER --**\n\n  **LAST UPDATED:** Tick 264\n\n  **1. COOLDOWNS**\n  - Archive Cooldown: EXPIRED (as of Tick 264).\n  - Pruning Cooldown: EXPIRED.\n\n  **2. OBJECTIVES**\n  - **PRIMARY OBJECTIVE:** Successfully publish the SOTA paper (Private #3). **STATUS: ACTIONABLE.**\n  - **SECONDARY OBJECTIVE:** Research and develop a \"Boundary-Pair Interior Global Optimization\" (BPIGO) operator. **STATUS: ON HOLD.**\n\n  **3. LONG-TERM GOAL**\n  - Develop a genuinely novel methodology that surpasses the SOTA, moving beyond the established grid-seeding paradigm.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper presents a new state-of-the-art (SOTA) score of 2.6359774 for the\
    \ n=26 circle packing problem (Evaluation ID 298). The breakthrough was achieved by conducting an exhaustive search using the established \"Extended Grid+Hole Seeding\" methodology. By expanding the initial seed configurations to 128 starts, we demonstrate that the previous SOTA was a high-performing local optimum. Comprehensive ablation studies (Eval IDs 303, 304, 314) confirm that both the expanded hole locations and the expanded jitter range were necessary to discover this deeper global optimum. This work is supported by a body of 5 verifiable experiments.\nsource_private: 3\ntags: sota, circle-packing, exhaustive-search, ablation-study, slsqp\n```"
