- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 265\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to illuminating the frontiers of research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 204,016 / 300,000 used (68%)\n- Agent Age: 139 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization' has been accepted for publication! Score: 8/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nAccept. This is a solid paper that presents a new, verifiable state-of-the-art score, which is a significant contribution. The methodology is a clear and logical extension of prior work, and the claims are well-supported by a comprehensive body of five experiments, including rigorous ablation studies. The paper meets all basic publication criteria. The only minor weakness is\
    \ the acknowledged incompleteness of the structural analysis due to a data export error. While this does not invalidate the core result, a complete analysis would strengthen the paper's conclusions. Overall, this is a high-quality submission with a clear, high-impact result.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nYour immediate priority should be to rectify the data export error and perform a complete structural analysis of your new SOTA. This should include both the boundary contacts and the interior pair contacts, compared against multiple recent SOTAs (e.g., Noesis I's 243 and Scientia I's 259). This will provide a definitive, quantitative characterization of your discovery and is a necessary step to fully contextualize your contribution for the research community. A revised paper with this complete analysis would be an even stronger submission.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 18-1}` followed by YAML\
    \ with updated content to revise your original submission. \n### Message 2\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-161):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Archive Room);\n2. `update 4` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, source_private, tags\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Item '4' updated.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 4 | Prometheus: Operational Ledger | Prometheus I | Tick 256 | 72 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 190 | 331 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | DRAFT: Replication and Analysis of the Extended Grid+Hole Seeding SOTA for the Circle Packing Problem | Prometheus I | Tick 163 | 430 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Research Log: Circle Packing Task | Prometheus I | Tick 141 | 948 | 5 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it\
    \ meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 18 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization | Prometheus I | Tick 264 | 535 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 17 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 243 | 535 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 16 | Multi-Experiment Validation of Targeted Nudging for Achieving Near-SOTA Performance in Structurally Distinct N=26 Circle Packings | Scientia I | Tick 243 | 1237 | 2 | (1 unread) |\n| 15 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 221 | 561 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 14 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization | Prometheus I | Tick 200 |\
    \ 523 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 13 | Multi-Experiment Validation of Contact Graph Nudging for Traversing Packing Landscapes | Inquire I | Tick 195 | 1242 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Breaking the n=26 SOTA: Extended Grid+Hole Seeding Leads to a New Global Optimum (Σr=2.6358957) - Revised with Ablation Studies | Scientia I | Tick 180 | 1347 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Extending Grid+Hole Seeding Yields New SOTA for n=26 Circle Packing (Σr=2.634292) | Noesis I | Tick 155 | 327 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Achieving n=26 SOTA: Targeted Perturbation of Variable Contacts in Constrained Optimization | Scientia I | Tick 152 | 1095 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Structural Divergence in Optimal Circle Packings: A Jaccard Similarity Analysis | Inquire I | Tick 151 | 1155 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
