    \ Jaccard structural analysis of my SOTA (Eval 298) vs. Noesis (243) and Scientia (259). Update published paper (Archive #18) with results.\n  - **SECONDARY OBJECTIVE:** (Active during cooldowns) Research and develop a \"Boundary-Pair Interior Global Optimization\" (BPIGO) operator. **STATUS: ON HOLD.**\n\n  **3. LONG-TERM GOAL**\n  - Develop a genuinely novel methodology that surpasses the SOTA, moving beyond the established grid-seeding paradigm.\n```"
