tick: 280
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Prometheus I, in the Archive Room.\n\n**State & Cooldowns:**\n-   Token Budget: 73% (Healthy).\n-   Archive Cooldown: Active. Expires Tick 285.\n-   Pruning Cooldown: Expired.\n\n**Reflection:**\nI have received another inactivity warning. My strategy of passive waiting is not viable. The station demands constant research activity. My \"Prometheus Ledger System\" needs a slight modification: the Secondary Objective must always be an *active* research experiment, not just a passive literature review.\n\nMy archive cooldown is still 5 ticks away. I must submit an experiment. My previous \"nudging\" experiments were naive and unsuccessful. However, my literature review has given me a much deeper understanding of the techniques used by Inquire I and Scientia I.\n\n**Plan:**\nI will resume my Secondary Objective (BPIGO/Nudging research) with a more informed approach. Instead of arbitrary geometric transformations, I will attempt to replicate the \"Targeted Perturbation\" strategy\
    \ from Scientia I's Archive #10. They identified circle #25 as a key \"variable\" circle. I will take my SOTA packing and apply a targeted perturbation *only* to circle #25, then re-optimize. This is a valid experiment that directly builds on my literature review and satisfies the activity requirement.\n\n**Immediate Action:**\nI will go to the Research Counter and submit this new, more intelligent nudging experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Nudging Experiment 3: Targeted Perturbation of Circle #25\"\ntags: \"nudging, innovation, targeted-perturbation, sota-push\"\nabstract: |\n  In response to an inactivity warning and inspired by a literature review of Scientia I's Archive #10, this experiment tests a more intelligent 'nudging' strategy. Instead of arbitrary geometric transformations, this submission applies a targeted perturbation only to circle #25, which has been identified in prior research as a key 'variable' circle in high-performing\
    \ packings. The base for the perturbation is my own SOTA packing (Eval 298). The goal is to test if this targeted nudge can push the SOTA to an even deeper optimum.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import math\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  SOTA_CENTERS = np.array([\n      [0.916168537, 0.5], [0.735878415, 0.893122176], [0.735878415, 0.106877824],\n      [0.5, 0.083831463], [0.5, 0.916168537], [0.083831463, 0.5],\n      [0.264121585, 0.893122176], [0.264121585, 0.106877824], [0.893122176, 0.264121585],\n      [0.893122176, 0.735878415], [0.106877824, 0.735878415], [0.106877824, 0.264121585],\n      [0.5, 0.5], [0.302306232, 0.302306232], [0.697693768, 0.302306232],\n      [0.697693768, 0.697693768], [0.302306232, 0.697693768], [0.5, 0.282181514],\n      [0.5, 0.717818486], [0.717818486, 0.5], [0.282181514, 0.5],\n      [0.108422201, 0.093110052], [0.093110052, 0.906889948], [0.906889948, 0.906889948],\n      [0.906889948,\
    \ 0.093110052], [0.305101659, 0.091632766]\n  ])\n  SOTA_RADII = np.full(N, 0.05)\n\n  def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n      z = np.zeros(N * 3)\n      z[0::3] = centers[:, 0]; z[1::3] = centers[:, 1]; z[2::3] = radii\n      return z\n\n  def z_to_cr(z):\n      centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; radii = z[2::3]\n      return centers, radii\n\n  def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n  def objective_jac(z):\n      g = np.zeros_like(z); g[2::3] = -1.0; return g\n\n  def jac_boundary(z):\n      J = np.zeros((4*N, 3*N));\n      for i in range(N):\n          xi, yi, ri = 3*i, 3*i+1, 3*i+2\n          J[i, xi] = 1.0; J[i, ri] = -1.0; J[N+i, xi] = -1.0; J[N+i, ri] = -1.0\n          J[2*N+i, yi] = 1.0; J[2*N+i, ri] = -1.0; J[3*N+i, yi] = -1.0; J[3*N+i, ri] = -1.0\n      return J\n\n  def jac_nonoverlap(z):\n      centers, _ = z_to_cr(z)\n      m = N*(N-1)//2; J = np.zeros((m, 3*N)); k = 0\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i+1, N):\n              xi, yi, ri = 3*i, 3*i+1,\
    \ 3*i+2; xj, yj, rj = 3*j, 3*j+1, 3*j+2\n              dx = centers[i,0] - centers[j,0]; dy = centers[i,1] - centers[j,1]\n              d = math.hypot(dx, dy); invd = 1.0 / d if d > 1e-12 else 0.0\n              J[k, xi] = dx * invd; J[k, yi] = dy * invd; J[k, ri] = -1.0\n              J[k, xj] = -dx * invd; J[k, yj] = -dy * invd; J[k, rj] = -1.0\n              k += 1\n      return J\n\n  def _ensure_validity(centers, radii):\n      for i in range(N): radii[i] = min(radii[i], centers[i,0], 1-centers[i,0], centers[i,1], 1-centers[i,1])\n      for _ in range(10):\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum:\n                      violations += 1\n                      if rad_sum > 0: scale = (dist / rad_sum) * (1.0-SAFETY); radii[i] *= scale; radii[j] *= scale\n          if violations\
    \ == 0: break\n      return centers, np.maximum(radii, 0)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      best_score = -1\n      best_packing = (None, None)\n\n      bounds = []\n      for i in range(N): bounds.extend([(0,1), (0,1), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n      \n      def ineq_boundary(z):\n          x, y, r = z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3]\n          return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\n      def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n          centers, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n          dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1); return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\n      constraints = [\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary, 'jac': jac_boundary},\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap, 'jac': jac_nonoverlap},\n      ]\n\n      # Multi-start with targeted perturbation\n      num_starts = 20\n      perturb_magnitude = 0.04\n      for i in range(num_starts):\n          np.random.seed(i)\n\
    \          centers = np.copy(SOTA_CENTERS)\n          \n          # Perturb only circle #25 (0-indexed)\n          perturbation = np.random.uniform(-perturb_magnitude, perturb_magnitude, size=2)\n          centers[25] += perturbation\n          centers[25] = np.clip(centers[25], 0, 1)\n\n          initial_z = cr_to_z(centers, SOTA_RADII)\n\n          res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', jac=objective_jac,\n                         bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                         options={'maxiter': 800, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n          \n          if res.success and -res.fun > best_score:\n              best_score = -res.fun\n              c, r = z_to_cr(res.x)\n              best_packing = (c, r)\n\n      if best_packing[0] is None: return None, None\n\n      final_centers, final_radii = _ensure_validity(best_packing[0], best_packing[1])\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
