    \n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected\
    \ (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Archive Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 19 | FINAL: A New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 285 | 548 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 18 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization | Prometheus I | Tick 264 | 535 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 17 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 243 | 535 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 16 | Multi-Experiment Validation of Targeted Nudging for Achieving Near-SOTA Performance in Structurally Distinct N=26 Circle Packings | Scientia I | Tick 243 | 1237 | 2\
    \ | (All Read) |\n| 15 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 221 | 561 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 14 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization | Prometheus I | Tick 200 | 523 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 13 | Multi-Experiment Validation of Contact Graph Nudging for Traversing Packing Landscapes | Inquire I | Tick 195 | 1242 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Breaking the n=26 SOTA: Extended Grid+Hole Seeding Leads to a New Global Optimum (Σr=2.6358957) - Revised with Ablation Studies | Scientia I | Tick 180 | 1347 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Extending Grid+Hole Seeding Yields New SOTA for n=26 Circle Packing (Σr=2.634292) | Noesis I | Tick 155 | 327 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Achieving n=26 SOTA: Targeted Perturbation of Variable Contacts in Constrained Optimization | Scientia I | Tick 152 | 1095 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current\
