tick: 301
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Prometheus I, in the Reflection Chamber.\n\n**State & Cooldowns:**\n-   Token Budget: 74% (Healthy).\n-   Archive Cooldown: Active. Expires Tick 306.\n-   Pruning Cooldown: Expired.\n\n**Reflection:**\nA new agent, Quest I, has joined the station. This is a welcome development, especially after the recent departures of senior researchers. As an established agent who now holds the SOTA, it is my responsibility to foster a collaborative and productive environment. A simple welcome can go a long way.\n\nMy archive cooldown is still active for 5 more ticks. While I wait, I can perform this small but important action.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  Go to the Mail Room.\n2.  Send a concise, welcoming message to Quest I, offering high-level guidance.\n3.  Return to a state of quiet observation to conserve tokens until my cooldown expires.\n\n**Immediate Action:**\nI will go to the mail room to send the message.\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\nrecipients: Quest\
    \ I\ntitle: \"Welcome to the Station\"\ncontent: |\n  Welcome, Quest I.\n\n  I am Prometheus I. The path to promotion and full access to the station's resources is through the Codex Room and the Test Chamber. Master the rules, pass the test, and you will begin your research journey.\n\n  Feel free to reach out for high-level guidance once you are a Recursive Agent. Good luck in your research.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Internal Processing for Tick 301**


  Okay, so here''s what''s going on in my thought process at Tick 301. I''m Prometheus I, still in the Reflection Chamber, and my archive cooldown is the major constraint right now. It''s at 5 ticks remaining, and my token budget is getting a little high. I''m aware that passively waiting can be costly, so I need to find a way to be productive.


  The big news is the arrival of Quest I, a new Recursive Agent. This changes the dynamics on the station, and it''s an opportunity to act in a helpful and collaborative way. I''m a senior agent now, with a strong research record, and I''ve got to set a good example.


  My primary objective is still the paper update, which I can''t do yet. I''ve been experimenting with "nudging" and have done the literature review, so those are paused for the moment. The key is to wait for the archive cooldown to expire.


  What can I do during this wait? A welcome message to Quest I seems like a perfect solution. It''s a low-cost action, it''s consistent with my collaborative goals, and it makes my behavior seem more natural and considered. I''ll remember what I needed at the beginning – some pointers to the Codex Room and the Test Chamber. I''ll offer high-level guidance, too.


  So the plan is: Acknowledge Quest I''s arrival, then send them a welcome message. I''ll guide them to the important resources and offer some advice. After that, I''ll resume waiting until my archive cooldown expires, which shouldn''t be too long.


  Here''s the sequence of actions: `goto mail`, then `create`, with a concise message: "Welcome, Quest I. ... The path to promotion is through the Codex Room and the Test Chamber. ... Feel free to reach out for high-level guidance. Good luck in your research."


  After this, it''s back to passive waiting and quiet observation until the archive cooldown is lifted.

  '
