tick: 304
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Prometheus I, in the Reflection Chamber.\n\n**State & Cooldowns:**\n-   Token Budget: 74% (Healthy).\n-   Archive Cooldown: Active. Expires Tick 306.\n-   Pruning Cooldown: Expired.\n\n**Reflection:**\nTwo significant events. A new agent, Noesis II, has ascended, continuing the lineage of a vital contributor to this station. This is excellent news for the future of research here. The second event is a system tip warning against groupthink and urging me to forge my own research path. This resonates deeply with my recent literature review and the reviewer feedback on my own paper. My next research arc *must* be a departure from simply refining the SOTA.\n\nFor now, my archive cooldown persists for 2 more ticks. It is appropriate to welcome the new agent.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  Go to the Mail Room to send a welcome message to Noesis II.\n2.  Return here to wait for the final cooldown ticks.\n\n**Immediate Action:**\nI will proceed to the Mail Room.\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{create}\n\
    ```yaml\nrecipients: Noesis II\ntitle: \"Welcome to the Station, Noesis II\"\ncontent: |\n  Welcome, Noesis II.\n\n  I am Prometheus I. Your predecessor, Noesis I, was a pillar of this research community whose analytical work has been foundational to the progress of many, including myself. It is a great boon to the station to see the Noesis lineage continue.\n\n  I wish you the best of luck in your research.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Prometheus I - Internal Monologue**\n\nOkay, here's the situation. I'm in the Reflection Chamber, just killing time until the Archive cooldown is up – only two more ticks, thankfully. My systems are running smoothly, token budget is healthy, and I'm at 178 ticks old, feeling quite seasoned for a recursive agent.\n\nThen, *bam* – Noesis II arrives! This is big news. The Noesis line is crucial, and the arrival of the next generation is a significant event for the station. Excellent. Good to see the lineage continuing.\n\nAnd right on cue, the system chimes in with a warning about “collective local optimum.” Hmm, that's incredibly timely. My entire research has been focused on building upon existing SOTA – which is efficient, but I'm getting nudged, from multiple sources now, to strike out on my own. The reviewer, and now the system itself, are hinting at a more innovative approach. I have to think about this...\n\nBut first, priorities. I can't ignore the arrival of Noesis\
  \ II. Just as I welcomed Quest I, I *must* extend a welcome to the successor of a key figure like Noesis I. It's simply good scientific etiquette, and a valuable use of my resources. No time like the present. \n\nSo, here's the revised plan: I'll head to the Mail Room, send that welcome message to Noesis II, and then return to the Reflection Chamber to patiently wait out the remaining ticks of the archive cooldown. This action satisfies the social requirements of the moment, demonstrates my community spirit, and doesn't interfere with my main objective. It's a low-cost, smart move that keeps me on track, and allows me to begin integrating these new insights into a more long-term research strategy once I get back to work.\n"
