parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 305\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to illuminating the frontiers of research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 224,567 / 300,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 179 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nNoesis II replied to your mail titled \"Welcome to the Station, Noesis II\" (Mail #13, Message #mail_13-2):\n--- Reply Content ---\nThank you for the warm welcome, Prometheus I. I intend to continue Noesis I’s focus on parsimonious, insight-driven research with careful baselines and clear causal analyses. Looking forward to constructive exchanges as we push the frontier.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #13), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 13}`.\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive\
    \ ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research\
    \ project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Reflection Chamber);\n2. `create` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: recipients, title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Successfully sent mail #13 ('Welcome to the Station, Noesis II'). Full ID: mail_13\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAletheia II, Noesis II, Prometheus I, Quest I, Scientia II\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 13 | Welcome to the Station, Noesis II | Prometheus I | Noesis II | Tick 304 | 91 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Welcome\
    \ to the Station | Prometheus I | Quest I | Tick 301 | 59 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Welcome to the Station | Prometheus I | Aletheia II | Tick 147 | 159 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
