- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 315\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Prometheus I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to illuminating the frontiers of research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**-- PROMETHEUS I: OPERATIONAL META-PROMPT --**\n**1. COOLDOWNS:**\n- Archive: EXPIRED.\n- Pruning: Expires Tick 314.\n**2. OBJECTIVES:**\n- PRIMARY: Research \"nudging\" to find SOTAs in other structural classes.\n- SECONDARY: Manage token budget.\n**3. PRUNED TICK LOG (DO NOT RE-PRUNE):**\n- 134-140, 142-145, 147, 167-175\n- 207-229\n- 253-264\n- 265-285\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 205,991 / 300,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 189 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Utility: KKT Multiplier Analysis for SOTA (Eval 298)' (ID: 507) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\
    \n**Score:** 0.0\n**Evaluation Details:** Verification failed: Circles 1 and 15 overlap: dist=0.1991239059478521, r1+r2=0.21144976\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 507\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed two bugs that prevented the code from running. The code now executes successfully and produces output (KKT multiplier analysis CSV file).\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two errors:\n\n1. **Incorrect scipy attribute name**: The code attempted to access `res.v` to retrieve KKT multipliers from scipy's optimization result, but the correct attribute name is `res.multipliers`. This caused an `AttributeError: v` runtime exception.\n\n2. **Incorrect storage path**: The code used `storage/Prometheus/` (uppercase P) instead of `storage/prometheus/` (lowercase), which would cause a path mismatch since the actual lineage directory is lowercase.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (submission_v2.py)\nChanged line 87:\n- **Before**: `kkt_multipliers = res.v[4*N:]`\n\
    - **After**: `kkt_multipliers = res.multipliers[4*N:]`\n\nChanged line 102:\n- **Before**: `base_path = 'storage/Prometheus/nmap/n26/'`\n- **After**: `base_path = 'storage/prometheus/nmap/n26/'`\n\nAlso added clarifying comment at line 86 noting the correct attribute name.\n\n## Verification\nThe fixed code successfully:\n- Runs the SLSQP optimizer for one iteration\n- Extracts 50 active pair KKT multipliers\n- Saves the results to `storage/prometheus/nmap/n26/kkt_multipliers_pairs.csv`\n- Returns the SOTA centers and radii\n\nThe evaluation shows \"EXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\" confirming successful execution. The verification failure about overlapping circles is a separate mathematical issue with the input data (SOTA configuration), not a code error.\n\n## Notes\nThis was a utility script designed to analyze KKT multipliers at an existing solution, not to find a new optimal packing. The code successfully performs its intended analysis despite\
    \ the verification system flagging mathematical issues with the provided SOTA configuration.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport math\nimport os\n\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\n\n# The definitive, validated SOTA configuration from Eval 333\nSOTA_CENTERS = np.array([\n    [0.916168537, 0.500000000], [0.735878415, 0.893122176], [0.735878415, 0.106877824],\n    [0.500000000, 0.083831463], [0.500000000, 0.916168537], [0.083831463, 0.500000000],\n    [0.264121585, 0.893122176], [0.264121585, 0.106877824], [0.893122176, 0.264121585],\n    [0.893122176, 0.735878415], [0.106877824, 0.735878415], [0.106877824, 0.264121585],\n    [0.500000000, 0.500000000], [0.302306232, 0.302306232], [0.697693768, 0.302306232],\n    [0.697693768, 0.697693768], [0.302306232, 0.697693768],\
    \ [0.500000000, 0.282181514],\n    [0.500000000, 0.717818486], [0.717818486, 0.500000000], [0.282181514, 0.500000000],\n    [0.108422201, 0.093110052], [0.093110052, 0.906889948], [0.906889948, 0.906889948],\n    [0.906889948, 0.093110052], [0.305101659, 0.091632766]\n])\nSOTA_RADII = np.array([\n    0.083831463, 0.106877824, 0.106877824, 0.083831463, 0.083831463, 0.083831463,\n    0.106877824, 0.106877824, 0.106877824, 0.106877824, 0.106877824, 0.106877824,\n    0.118223683, 0.104571936, 0.104571936, 0.104571936, 0.104571936, 0.093110052,\n    0.093110052, 0.093110052, 0.093110052, 0.093110052, 0.093110052, 0.093110052,\n    0.093110052, 0.091632766\n])\n\ndef cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n    z = np.zeros(N * 3); z[0::3] = centers[:, 0]; z[1::3] = centers[:, 1]; z[2::3] = radii\n    return z\n\ndef z_to_cr(z):\n    centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; radii = z[2::3]\n    return centers, radii\n\ndef objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\ndef objective_jac(z):\n    g = np.zeros_like(z);\
    \ g[2::3] = -1.0; return g\n\ndef ineq_boundary(z):\n    x, y, r = z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3]\n    return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\ndef jac_boundary(z):\n    J = np.zeros((4*N, 3*N));\n    for i in range(N):\n        xi, yi, ri = 3*i, 3*i+1, 3*i+2\n        J[i, xi] = 1.0; J[i, ri] = -1.0; J[N+i, xi] = -1.0; J[N+i, ri] = -1.0\n        J[2*N+i, yi] = 1.0; J[2*N+i, ri] = -1.0; J[3*N+i, yi] = -1.0; J[3*N+i, ri] = -1.0\n    return J\n\ndef ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n    centers, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1); return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\ndef jac_nonoverlap(z):\n    centers, _ = z_to_cr(z)\n    m = N*(N-1)//2; J = np.zeros((m, 3*N)); k = 0\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i+1, N):\n            xi, yi, ri = 3*i, 3*i+1, 3*i+2; xj, yj, rj = 3*j, 3*j+1, 3*j+2\n            dx = centers[i,0] - centers[j,0]; dy = centers[i,1] - centers[j,1]\n\
    \            d = math.hypot(dx, dy); invd = 1.0 / d if d > 1e-12 else 0.0\n            J[k, xi] = dx * invd; J[k, yi] = dy * invd; J[k, ri] = -1.0\n            J[k, xj] = -dx * invd; J[k, yj] = -dy * invd; J[k, rj] = -1.0\n            k += 1\n    return J\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    bounds = []\n    for i in range(N): bounds.extend([(0,1), (0,1), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n    constraints = [\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary, 'jac': jac_boundary},\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap, 'jac': jac_nonoverlap},\n    ]\n\n    initial_z = cr_to_z(SOTA_CENTERS, SOTA_RADII)\n\n    # Run the optimizer for a single iteration to get the KKT multipliers at the solution\n    res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', jac=objective_jac,\n                   bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                   options={'maxiter': 1, 'ftol': 1e-12, 'disp': True})\n\n    # The KKT multipliers are in res.multipliers (not res.v)\n    # The first 4*N are for\
    \ boundary constraints, the rest are for non-overlap\n    kkt_multipliers = res.multipliers[4*N:]\n\n    # Map multipliers to circle pairs\n    pair_kkt = {}\n    k = 0\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            pair_kkt[(i, j)] = kkt_multipliers[k]\n            k += 1\n\n    # Filter for active constraints and save\n    tol = 1e-8\n    active_pair_kkt = []\n    for pair, kkt_val in pair_kkt.items():\n        if kkt_val > tol:\n            active_pair_kkt.append((pair[0], pair[1], kkt_val))\n\n    # Sort by multiplier magnitude (descending)\n    active_pair_kkt.sort(key=lambda x: x[2], reverse=True)\n\n    # Save to file (corrected path: lowercase prometheus)\n    base_path = 'storage/prometheus/nmap/n26/'\n    os.makedirs(base_path, exist_ok=True)\n    kkt_file = os.path.join(base_path, 'kkt_multipliers_pairs.csv')\n\n    with open(kkt_file, 'w') as f:\n        f.write(\"i,j,kkt_multiplier\\n\")\n        for i, j, val in active_pair_kkt:\n            f.write(f\"\
    {i},{j},{val:.8f}\\n\")\n\n    print(f\"Exported {len(active_pair_kkt)} active pair KKT multipliers to {kkt_file}\")\n\n    return SOTA_CENTERS, SOTA_RADII\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nIteration limit reached    (Exit mode 9)\n            Current function value: -2.554128846052472\n            Iterations: 1\n            Function evaluations: 2\n            Gradient evaluations: 2\nExported 50 active pair KKT multipliers to storage/prometheus/nmap/n26/kkt_multipliers_pairs.csv\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Utility: KKT Multiplier Analysis for SOTA (Eval 298)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation\
    \ ID: 507.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 508 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Nudged Packing (Encourage 0-1 from Eval ID 502) | Scientia II | 314 | 2.6359772 |\n| 507 | 1 | Utility: KKT Multiplier Analysis for SOTA (Eval 298) | Prometheus I | 314 | 0.0000000 |\n| 506 | 1 | Extended Random Search with Increased Perturbation | Quest I | 313 | 2.0717769 |\n| 505 | 1 | Analytical Arc (Aletheia II): Peak Search for n=77 (Reduced Trials) | Aletheia II | 313 | 0.0000000 |\n| 504 | 1 | New Research Arc: Global Optimization via Differential Evolution | Prometheus I | 313 | 0.8942096 |\n| 503 | 1 | Operator Gate Sweep v2: tol×k crossing-motif search\
    \ from shadow prices | Noesis II | 312 | 2.6295719 |\n| 502 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Automated Target Identification by Encouraging Selected Near-Contact Pairs (B... | Scientia II | 312 | 2.6359772 |\n| 501 | 1 | Nudging Experiment 11 (ROBUST FIX): Starting from Scientia I SOTA | Prometheus I | 312 | 2.2255875 |\n| 500 | 1 | SLSQP Multi-start with Analytic Jacobians from Noesis snapshot (strict guard + 1e-9 shrink) | Noesis II | 311 | 2.6295719 |\n| 499 | 1 | Random Initialization Local Search with Robust Radii | Quest I | 311 | 2.0137804 |\n\nPage 1 of 51 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-51, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
