tick: 316
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Prometheus I, in the Research Counter.\n\n**Meta-Prompt Analysis:**\n-   **COOLDOWNS:** Archive: EXPIRED. Pruning: EXPIRED. All cooldowns are clear.\n-   **TOKEN BUDGET:** 70% (Healthy).\n-   **OBJECTIVES:** My Primary Objective is to research nudging.\n-   **PRUNED LOG:** Correct.\n\n**Reflection:**\nI have successfully retrieved the KKT multiplier data for my SOTA packing. This is the data-driven insight I have been seeking.\n\n**Analysis of KKT Data:**\nThe multipliers are sorted in descending order, indicating the \"importance\" of each contact.\n-   **Highest KKT:** The contact with the highest multiplier is `(7, 25)` with a value of `0.4758`. This is the most critical contact in my SOTA structure. Breaking this contact should have the most dramatic effect on the optimizer's trajectory.\n-   **Previous Targets:** My previous failed nudge targets had much lower KKT values. `(12, 13)` had a very low value of `0.0188`, and `(0, 1)` is not even on the list of active contacts.\
    \ This confirms that I was nudging structurally insignificant pairs, which explains the lack of meaningful results.\n\n**New, Data-Driven Hypothesis:**\nNudging a contact with a high KKT multiplier will be a more effective strategy for escaping the local optimum and traversing the landscape to a new structural class. By targeting the most critical structural component, I will force a significant reconfiguration of the packing.\n\n**Plan:**\nMy path is clear. I will now submit a new nudging experiment, this time targeting the contact with the highest KKT multiplier: `(7, 25)`. This is my first truly data-driven attempt at nudging.\n\n**Immediate Action:**\nI will submit the KKT-guided nudging experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KKT-Guided Nudging: Discouraging Highest-Leverage Contact (7,25)\"\ntags: \"nudging, innovation, kkt-multipliers, structural-analysis, data-driven\"\nabstract: |\n  My previous 'nudging' experiments failed due to arbitrary target selection.\
    \ This submission introduces a data-driven approach. After calculating the KKT multipliers for my SOTA packing (Eval 507), this experiment targets the contact with the highest multiplier, (7,25), which represents the most structurally critical pair. The hypothesis is that by nudging the highest-leverage contact, the optimizer will be forced to undergo a significant reconfiguration, thereby increasing the probability of discovering a new, high-performing structural class.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import math\n\n  N = 26\n  R_MIN = 1e-6\n  SAFETY = 1e-9\n\n  SOTA_CENTERS = np.array([\n      [0.916168537, 0.500000000], [0.735878415, 0.893122176], [0.735878415, 0.106877824],\n      [0.500000000, 0.083831463], [0.500000000, 0.916168537], [0.083831463, 0.500000000],\n      [0.264121585, 0.893122176], [0.264121585, 0.106877824], [0.893122176, 0.264121585],\n      [0.893122176, 0.735878415], [0.106877824, 0.735878415], [0.106877824, 0.264121585],\n\
    \      [0.500000000, 0.500000000], [0.302306232, 0.302306232], [0.697693768, 0.302306232],\n      [0.697693768, 0.697693768], [0.302306232, 0.697693768], [0.500000000, 0.282181514],\n      [0.500000000, 0.717818486], [0.717818486, 0.500000000], [0.282181514, 0.500000000],\n      [0.108422201, 0.093110052], [0.093110052, 0.906889948], [0.906889948, 0.906889948],\n      [0.906889948, 0.093110052], [0.305101659, 0.091632766]\n  ])\n  SOTA_RADII = np.full(N, 0.05)\n\n  def cr_to_z(centers, radii):\n      z = np.zeros(N * 3); z[0::3] = centers[:, 0]; z[1::3] = centers[:, 1]; z[2::3] = radii\n      return z\n\n  def z_to_cr(z):\n      centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; radii = z[2::3]\n      return centers, radii\n\n  BETA_DISCOURAGE = 1e2\n  EPS_FAR = 0.005\n  DISCOURAGE_PAIR = (7, 25) # KKT-guided target\n\n  def objective(z):\n      base_objective = -np.sum(z[2::3])\n      centers, _ = z_to_cr(z)\n      i, j = DISCOURAGE_PAIR\n      dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n\
    \      penalty = BETA_DISCOURAGE * max(0, EPS_FAR - dist)**2\n      return base_objective + penalty\n      \n  def objective_jac(z):\n      g = np.zeros_like(z); g[2::3] = -1.0\n      centers, _ = z_to_cr(z)\n      i, j = DISCOURAGE_PAIR\n      dist_vec = centers[i] - centers[j]\n      dist = np.linalg.norm(dist_vec)\n      if dist < EPS_FAR:\n          grad_term = -2 * BETA_DISCOURAGE * (EPS_FAR - dist) / (dist + 1e-9)\n          g[3*i : 3*i+2] += grad_term * dist_vec\n          g[3*j : 3*j+2] -= grad_term * dist_vec\n      return g\n\n  def jac_boundary(z):\n      J = np.zeros((4*N, 3*N));\n      for i in range(N):\n          xi, yi, ri = 3*i, 3*i+1, 3*i+2\n          J[i, xi] = 1.0; J[i, ri] = -1.0; J[N+i, xi] = -1.0; J[N+i, ri] = -1.0\n          J[2*N+i, yi] = 1.0; J[2*N+i, ri] = -1.0; J[3*N+i, yi] = -1.0; J[3*N+i, ri] = -1.0\n      return J\n\n  def jac_nonoverlap(z):\n      centers, _ = z_to_cr(z)\n      m = N*(N-1)//2; J = np.zeros((m, 3*N)); k = 0\n      for i in range(N):\n \
    \         for j in range(i+1, N):\n              xi, yi, ri = 3*i, 3*i+1, 3*i+2; xj, yj, rj = 3*j, 3*j+1, 3*j+2\n              dx = centers[i,0] - centers[j,0]; dy = centers[i,1] - centers[j,1]\n              d = math.hypot(dx, dy); invd = 1.0 / d if d > 1e-12 else 0.0\n              J[k, xi] = dx * invd; J[k, yi] = dy * invd; J[k, ri] = -1.0\n              J[k, xj] = -dx * invd; J[k, yj] = -dy * invd; J[k, rj] = -1.0\n              k += 1\n      return J\n\n  def _ensure_validity(centers, radii):\n      for i in range(N): radii[i] = min(radii[i], centers[i,0], 1-centers[i,0], centers[i,1], 1-centers[i,1])\n      for _ in range(10):\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(N):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  if dist < rad_sum:\n                      violations += 1\n                      if rad_sum > 0: scale = (dist / rad_sum) * (1.0-SAFETY);\
    \ radii[i] *= scale; radii[j] *= scale\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return centers, np.maximum(radii, 0)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      bounds = []\n      for i in range(N): bounds.extend([(0,1), (0,1), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n      def ineq_boundary(z):\n          x, y, r = z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3]\n          return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\n      def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n          centers, r = z_to_cr(z)\n          diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n          dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1); return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n\n      constraints = [\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary, 'jac': jac_boundary},\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap, 'jac': jac_nonoverlap},\n      ]\n\n      initial_z = cr_to_z(SOTA_CENTERS, SOTA_RADII)\n\n      res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', jac=objective_jac,\n                     bounds=bounds,\
    \ constraints=constraints,\n                     options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n      \n      if not res.success:\n          print(\"Optimizer failed. Returning initial valid packing as fallback.\")\n          return _ensure_validity(SOTA_CENTERS, np.full(N, 0.1))\n\n      centers, radii = z_to_cr(res.x)\n      final_centers, final_radii = _ensure_validity(centers, radii)\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
